atars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T12:15:29-07:00","id":1461253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461252#post1461252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd make a snappy rhetorical question but you'd take it seriously and somehow write a list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, my favorites are mostly the OPP V5 stuff. I freely admit that I think the best creations of the V5 era are 3rd party and it started on the wrong foot, IMHO.<br /> <br /> LA By Night, Comics, Coteries of New York/Shadows of New York, and the Chicago by Night/Blood Cults stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T13:13:58-07:00","id":1461261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461227#post1461227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see less the chance that Gaia could die and more the possibility that she's the victim of something awful and traumatic and will take a long time to pick herself back together and the Garou have to rescue her from this cruel fate, save her from big bad daddy wyrm, and rehabilitate her while she's in anguish.<br /> <br /> I mean if you're going to gender the planet and the forces of maintenance and destruction you might as well use it right? (Did they give the wyld a gender? I mean it's birthing a lot but it's also a mess but also why is the prime evil one a male but also... I'm getting ahead of myself.) IDK talking about gender and WTA is certainly something that's burned me before. But I find the idea of a caring mother earth/mother nature laughable when nature is so damn scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia is complicated, or at least, loves such a wide variety that the ensuing issues aren't something she can really step into and intervene on too directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T14:41:14-07:00","id":1461272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461227#post1461227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">she's the victim of something awful and traumatic and will take a long time to pick herself back together and the Garou have to rescue her from this cruel fate, save her from big bad daddy wyrm, and rehabilitate her while she's in anguish.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Warriors of Gaia will face their greatest challenge of all? Become nurses, physical therapists and social workers?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461235#post1461235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see why people are concerned with the changes in metaplot etc. but I'm not particularly bothered for the simple reason that what interests me in W5 (and eventually M5 and C5) is the rules not the metaplot. I like the rules of V5 far more than those of the 20th Anniversary games</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally didn't liked the Disciplines a lot, and I'm not just talking about Oblivion. But yeah, otherwise it is a good change of system, although I still find Requiem 2nd better and prefer to use the Translation Guide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461261#post1461261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia is complicated, or at least, loves such a wide variety that the ensuing issues aren't something she can really step into and intervene on too directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia faces the same problem of every RPG god. She can't take care of things, otherwise we wouldn't have a game to play.<br /> <br /> On my part and in all sincerity, I can't agree with most directions of the new stuff but I can't say that everything is horrible, either. And the rules aren't bad at all. But it just feels like they couldn't decide how to engage the project. Every one of the big changes strike me as half made, trying to change everything but fearing changing too much. Changes that I really disliked? Only nuCamarilla, I really find it a bad change, not because the result is a stupid sect, but because it seems out of character. Extremely out of character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T21:55:55-07:00","id":1461302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461249#post1461249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shame. You're missing some fantastic stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> Whenever I talk about V5 (and I it looks like this will be my sentiment re- W5, and probably M5 if the trend holds,) I try to not make value judgments about it because, by all indications, there are a lot of people who really enjoy the game--and even better, people who would never have played any tabletop RPG if not for V5. It just isn't a game I'm particularly interested in playing for a bunch of reasons I won't get into, but that basically boil down to matters of personal taste and preference (as opposed to a sentiment about the <i>quality </i>of the design and writing.) Similarly, I'm positive that Call of Cthulhu is a great game (a jillion people can't just be <i>wrong</i>)--but it simply isn't my idea of fun or a good time. The same goes for baseball, poker, Candy Crush, and bunch of other games; I'm not going to call them bad, but they're not for me.<br /> <br /> So, please know that I'm sincere when I say that I'm sure these 5th Ed. games are someone's (many someones') idea of fantastic, and I wish those folks a million hours of fun playing. But it's going to be a 'no' for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T22:03:36-07:00","id":1461304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461302#post1461302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Whenever I talk about V5 (and I it looks like this will be my sentiment re- W5, and probably M5 if the trend holds,) I try to not make value judgments about it because, by all indications, there are a lot of people who really enjoy the game--and even better, people who would never have played any tabletop RPG if not for V5. It just isn't a game I'm particularly interested in playing for a bunch of reasons I won't get into, but that basically boil down to matters of personal taste and preference (as opposed to a sentiment about the <i>quality </i>of the design and writing.) Similarly, I'm positive that Call of Cthulhu is a great game (a jillion people can't just be <i>wrong</i>)--but it simply isn't my idea of fun or a good time. The same goes for baseball, poker, Candy Crush, and bunch of other games; I'm not going to call them bad, but they're not for me.<br /> <br /> So, please know that I'm sincere when I say that I'm sure these 5th Ed. games are someone's (many someones') idea of fantastic, and I wish those folks a million hours of fun playing. But it's going to be a 'no' for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. Life is too short to force yourself to try to like something you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T02:58:19-07:00","id":1461532,"title":"","content":"What will come first W5 or Chronicles? Any release dates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T03:24:41-07:00","id":1461537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461532#post1461532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What will come first W5 or Chronicles? Any release dates?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Almost certainly Chronicles considering the short time W5 has been with the current development team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T11:39:30-07:00","id":1461583,"title":"","content":"In case anyone prefers a physical copy and/or hates Amazon as much as I do, the comic book is currently slated to come out on October 13, with issue 2 on October 27, and issue three on December 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T01:47:39-07:00","id":1461650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461108#post1461108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the main take away here and elsewhere is a bunch of folks who never liked WtA or don't know much about it think this sounds ' vaguely interesting' and those of us that love and play the game are deeply worried.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the WoD alsways lacked some coherence. A &quot;Bible&quot; like Star Wars and Star Trek have so that the editors can say what goes and what doesn't - and what is &quot;elseworlds&quot; or so.<br /> <br /> So, just like when W20 came and changed things (that I find irreconcilable with the game I played till then), I think that the W5 authors (or the BNS authors, who I met in New Orleans and Berlin) don't work in bad faith, but are working on a game that they like to play and incorporate elements they developed during their their games. And possibly Paradox is demanding some changes, for they aim to go multi-media and certain elements of the games need to change, potentially, to develop broadcasting options or something like that.<br /> <br /> The problem is, that they seem to work in some kind of confirmation bubble. They might get feedback from players somewhere, read some forums, but they aren't open about it (well, I guess, I didn't follow news that close anymore, unlike when nuWW came to be).<br /> <br /> Well, we as players aren't included it the development process, so for some of us the game is developed failing to meet our needs or expectations. Then again, these needs and expectations might differ greatly among all the players.<br /> <br /> I for example, have no problem with a lot of the political incorrectness that the game has, while others feel changes should be made, for example re-nameing game elements like Metis. So, it is difficult to make it right.<br /> <br /> Yet, it is my fear, that the game is going into a direction that I don't want to play anymore. Maybe, I should then publish my own stuff via Storyteller's Vault...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T09:16:55-07:00","id":1461699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461650#post1461650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, we as players aren't included it the development process, so for some of us the game is developed failing to meet our needs or expectations. Then again, these needs and expectations might differ greatly among all the players.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think your statement about 'differ greatly among all the players' is spot-on. The developers are, ostensibly, WoD players (or were at one time.) The game(s) they're making are probably purpose-built to be very good at telling the kinds of stories (and in the style,) <i>they</i> liked to play. Anyone who isn't immediately down with the new direction can either learn to like it, or kick rocks--it is what it is. But I think it would be a mistake to write off the changes to the games as being totally divorced from player input or desire. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461650#post1461650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I for example, have no problem with a lot of the political incorrectness that the game has, while others feel changes should be made, for example re-nameing game elements like Metis. So, it is difficult to make it right.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nothing in the first four editions of the WoD particularly ruffled my feathers--but I'm also not a member of any of the groups who would have been in a position to feel offended or otherwise take umbrage. That said, I still haven't encountered a change to the WoD made for ostensible 'political correctness' reasons that bothered me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461650#post1461650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet, it is my fear, that the game is going into a direction that I don't want to play anymore. Maybe, I should then publish my own stuff via Storyteller's Vault...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> <i>That's</i> the spirit!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T12:43:53-07:00","id":1462464,"title":"","content":"Hi primary mage player here in regards to idea of all the caerns being gone Correct me if I'm wrong but<br /> <br /> 1) isn't there a rite to make more?<br /> 2) isn't a caern just a node controlled by werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-02-2021, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T13:46:15-07:00","id":1462475,"title":"","content":"Keeping in mind that (a) the W5 people haven't actually said anything about Caerns and I brought it up because it's part of the BNS material and (b) a lot of WtA fans did not like the changes BNS introduced...<br /> <br /> 1) The Rite still has prerequisites. The Garou can't just turn any Node into a Caern, they require Nodes with specific sympathies and resonances that align with their spiritual magic. This is one of the reasons the Garou don't like mages, who can turn any Caern into a Node, but they can't do the reverse, giving mages a huge advantage in any fight over such locations. The Rite is also exceptionally hard (pre-W20 is was effectively impossible without ST fiat due to the mechanics, and W20 just made it really hard to do instead), and sets off a giant spiritual signal flare to all of the Garou's enemies nearby that now is a perfect time to attack them.<br /> <br /> Basically, while making new Caerns is possible, there's a good reason (even before various metaplot events) why the Garou focus on strengthening and defending the ones they have, rather than trying to create as many as possible.<br /> <br /> 2) On top of what I noted about, in Mage terms, the requirements a Node needs to be a valid Caern, the magic used by the Garou to open a Caern transforms it into something distinct from other Nodes. Once the Caern is successfully opened, it has it's own spiritual patron (who can pass out extra powers to some of those working for it), can be linked to other Caerns via Moonbridges, and are subject to a whole set of Rites that only work on or near a Caern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T03:24:22-07:00","id":1462540,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I get th</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">at but it could be </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">an interesting plot point if the G</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">arou n</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">ation is pro</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">actively </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">attempting to </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">acquire nodes </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">as opposed to sitting around feeling sorry for themselves. I me</span></span></span>an in previous editions these things were a warrior race determined to go down swinging as the odds looked increasingly bleak and even then they were still in the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-03-2021, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T03:44:04-07:00","id":1462542,"title":"","content":"It's not really that interesting in the themes of WtA. WtA has strong themes of fatalism (it's the Apocalypse and all) and spirituality, which are served by Caerns being under threat. Having it be more tactically intuitive to hold the ones they have instead of trying to make more supports the themes of the game in a fashion where getting them more easily wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Caerns aren't just magical springs of energy to treat as a resource. They're holy and sacred to the PCs who are members of a religious fanatic organization. Trivializing them into just being any old Node to storm in and take over undermines huge swaths of the Garou faith.<br /> <br /> It's also really not fair to categorize them as &quot;sitting around feeling sorry for themselves,&quot; just because they're on the defensive militarily regarding Caerns. The Garou are fighting a much large war on multiple fronts. Some battles they're on the offense, some they're on the defense. And it's all going out and doing stuff, not sitting around doing nothing.<br /> <br /> What you're suggesting is about on par, Watsonianly, with suggesting that a religious person shouldn't be upset that someone tried to burn their treasured family heirloom holy books, when they could spend their time collecting rare books of any sort instead. Or in Mage terms, you're kinda sounding like a Hermetic suggesting that a Dreamspeaker should stop &quot;feeling sorry for themselves,&quot; because they're fighting to preserve indigenous cultures at risk of being destroyed by the ongoing impact of colonialism, and instead should go find new cultures to base their magical practices on that aren't at risk of getting wiped out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T11:43:38-07:00","id":1462571,"title":"","content":"Even then, the idea of recovering holy sites isn't all that bad for a new take on the setting, and W5 should be a new take anyways. It isn't about getting <i>any</i> node, but finding suitable ones, uncovering their history to identify which ones are holy sites tainted by the Mages, and then try their damned best to retake, cleanse, restore and protect those sites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T12:14:20-07:00","id":1462577,"title":"","content":"I saw Magical Werewolf Sadness open for Queensryche in New Haven one time, and they tore the roof off it.<br /> <br /> In any event, reading all of this reminds me of the developer quote from a couple years back (I wish I could find a link, I really tried), just after ownership changed hands and plans for 5th editions of the games were announced, that the Technocracy had lost the Ascension War and the Nephandi had won.<br /> <br /> A world in an ongoing state of crisis seems like it could be a theme for the entire 5th edition line, inspired by the state of the real world nearly twenty years after the end of the Revised editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T12:27:13-07:00","id":1462579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462571#post1462571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... and W5 should be a new take anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is something people probably don't agree on.<br /> But since V5 changed a lot of VtM and the reasons for the changes were driven by different needs of authors, game designers, IP owners and so on... so, W5 will probably, too.<br /> <br /> By Night Studios' version of WtA (which I would dub Age of Apocalypse) catered to the needs of the BNS hosted LARPs and the players and STs, as well as the &quot;coolness&quot; factor, that then-Head ST Martin Ericsson collaborated on the Setting (or was he still at CCP back then, can't say).<br /> <br /> <br /> I, for my tabletop games, would need a game system that is more &quot;modern&quot; than the Storyteller system of revised is. The Storyteller System was derived from the Shadowrun system back in the day when rolling huge amounts of dices was cool. But the resolution of rolls takes too long in my opinion, combat is often not delivering the drama needed, several mechanics don't fit with the gameplay and game world description and there are several other things I'd like to see addressed. Multiple actions need to go.<br /> <br /> But besides that, I don't need or want an update to the Setting. I don't want to address the names of tribes, don't need tribes to change to a level of what seems politically correct in 2021 and a lot of other suggested changes. I also don't need massive changes due to the 2nd Inquisition and stuff like that. The avatarstorm didn't affect WtA that much, so....<br /> <br /> There are some elements of W20 I would like to have reset to revised edition or 2nd Edition....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T13:12:51-07:00","id":1462582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462571#post1462571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, the idea of recovering holy sites isn't all that bad for a new take on the setting,...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a new take though In the WtA &quot;historical&quot; settings, this is a more prominent aspect of the game (even if more from each other than from mages) because the Garou being played aren't seeing signs of The End all around them. Even then, it's still part of the modern day setting, just downplayed because of the imminent nature of the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Whether an increased focus on reclaiming Caerns is a good or bad element depends entirely on what the new take on the setting is. It's just hard to imagine a lot of situations where it's a good thing to refocus on that doesn't end up diminishing a lot of what's important about WtA to its fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T19:30:04-07:00","id":1462602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462577#post1462577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw Magical Werewolf Sadness open for Queensryche in New Haven one time, and they tore the roof off it....</div> </div> </div> </div>At Toad's Place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T19:48:20-07:00","id":1462604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462579#post1462579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is something people probably don't agree on.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is inevitable. Actually and truly inevitable.<br /> <br /> We don't live in the same time, and the writers won't be the same. The public isn't the same given how much even old players changed in this time. And there is the metaplot thing, something WoD can't escape because it is what drives the sells. And finally, the conditions of today's market. Not changing the take of the game just isn't an option, and trying to not change actually invites the author to not be aware of changes and get an even worse result.<br /> <br /> And people will have many disagreements. <b>You</b> may not want many of those changes to the setting, but many others do. There are real people that feel offended by some things in the setting with reason and are players too. Most people want updates in the setting. In fact, it is probable that more people will buy only for the updates to the setting than for the updates to the rules. Finally, going back is easier than going forward. Fans that want just new rules can use old lore, but new lore won't exist if they don't put it in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T19:57:37-07:00","id":1462605,"title":"","content":"&quot;Metaplot agnostic&quot; worked for some gamers and drove off others. Some are here for the rules, some are here for the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T20:45:48-07:00","id":1462607,"title":"","content":"I do hope that W5 introduces a new Tribe like V5 introduced the Hecata, even if it isn't great it'll be interesting at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T21:27:23-07:00","id":1462614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zahana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462602#post1462602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Toad's Place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell yeah, were you there?!? ROFLMAO","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T22:17:31-07:00","id":1462622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462607#post1462607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope that W5 introduces a new Tribe like V5 introduced the Hecata, even if it isn't great it'll be interesting at least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Hecata aren't new they're just a smushing together of a bunch of bloodlines that hate each other.....which was kinda annoying as it reduced the opportunities of play each offered individually. <br /> <br /> Closest equivalent in WtA would be if a bunch of Ronin somehow managed to convince a spirit to become their totem.....but we already have the Skin Dancers and Minotaur so that would be a bit of retreading the same ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T00:33:27-07:00","id":1462625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462605#post1462605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Metaplot agnostic&quot; worked for some gamers and drove off others. Some are here for the rules, some are here for the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think people that didn't bother with the X20 books for being &quot;metaplot agnostic,&quot; were driven off in quite the same way as V5 drove away a lot of older fans. As the 20th line grew, even if it avoided advancing a specific metaplot, it kept putting out more material that would be valuable to fans of the metaplot. There isn't the level of animus I'd expect to see for something that lives up to the idea of &quot;driven off,&quot; since that implies actively made people feel unwelcome as customers of the brand. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462607#post1462607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope that W5 introduces a new Tribe like V5 introduced the Hecata, even if it isn't great it'll be interesting at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>WtA has too many Tribes as it is, and lacks a concept like Bloodlines where you can compress a bunch of small groups into one larger group. More Tribes means it's harder to give each Tribe nuance and depth, and it just pressures them harder into the 1e shallow stereotypes they started as. It also furthers instead of lessens how much each Tribe is so defined by human cultural values instead of a blending of human, wolf, and Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T01:00:23-07:00","id":1462628,"title":"","content":"That's fair. Well, I do hope the mechanics in W5 are good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T01:50:54-07:00","id":1462629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462625#post1462625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think people that didn't bother with the X20 books for being &quot;metaplot agnostic,&quot; were driven off in quite the same way as V5 drove away a lot of older fans. As the 20th line grew, even if it avoided advancing a specific metaplot, it kept putting out more material that would be valuable to fans of the metaplot. There isn't the level of animus I'd expect to see for something that lives up to the idea of &quot;driven off,&quot; since that implies actively made people feel unwelcome as customers of the brand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that kind of comparison isn't really helpful because it is also two different kinds of interest. People who weren't interested in metaplot agnoticism because they didn't advance the setting didn't buy the books. People who hated V5 changes disliked the books because they changed things. One is a lack of interest and the other is anger over changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WtA has too many Tribes as it is, and lacks a concept like Bloodlines where you can compress a bunch of small groups into one larger group. More Tribes means it's harder to give each Tribe nuance and depth, and it just pressures them harder into the 1e shallow stereotypes they started as. It also furthers instead of lessens how much each Tribe is so defined by human cultural values instead of a blending of human, wolf, and Garou. </div> </div> </div>I always thought the differences among the Garou would be the caerns that would have their own cultures and histories. Also regional differences in tribes. Rage Across Russia did a good job with the Get of Fenris for example because in Russia they were known not as a bunch of bloodthirsty berserkers but loyal honorable soldiers who were significantly more trustworthy than the Silver Fangs they served.<br /> <br /> Sort of the SF's version of Trolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T03:13:40-07:00","id":1462634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462604#post1462604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is inevitable. Actually and truly inevitable.<br /> <br /> We don't live in the same time...., and the writers won't be the same. The public isn't the same given how much even old players changed in this time. And there is the metaplot thing, something WoD can't escape because it is what drives the sells. And finally, the conditions of today's market. Not changing the take of the game just isn't an option, and trying to not change actually invites the author to not be aware of changes and get an even worse result.<br /> <br /> And people will have many disagreements. <b>You</b> may not want many of those changes to the setting, but many others do. There are real people that feel offended by some things in the setting with reason and are players too. Most people want updates in the setting. In fact, it is probable that more people will buy only for the updates to the setting than for the updates to the rules. Finally, going back is easier than going forward. Fans that want just new rules can use old lore, but new lore won't exist if they don't put it in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you might be right, that changes are inevitable, since the IP owners demand them - and have more things in mind than just the tabletop RPG.<br /> <br /> I can see, that many others want this or that to change. I want things to change, too. If really a majority wants updates to the setting is disputable, but even if this is true, there is no representative study I know of on what changes people would like to see, how deep they cut into the game, or if these changes come in form of metaplot development or retcons.<br /> <br /> I can only remember W20 Changing Breeds as a book where there was really a possibility to directly comment on the written text and make suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T03:19:39-07:00","id":1462635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462629#post1462629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought the differences among the Garou would be the caerns that would have their own cultures and histories. Also regional differences in tribes. Rage Across Russia did a good job with the Get of Fenris for example because in Russia they were known not as a bunch of bloodthirsty berserkers but loyal honorable soldiers who were significantly more trustworthy than the Silver Fangs they served.<br /> <br /> Sort of the SF's version of Trolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st Edition and parts of 2nd Edition were more focused on local septs than on global affairs. This shifted with revised, the global metaplot, and continued on in W20.<br /> <br /> I usually try to have elements of the tribal culture influence the local sept culture. But sure, even with two Get septs, culture can be very different...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T03:23:18-07:00","id":1462636,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Paradoxs development of W5 ( and V5) is very much behind closed doors....its a marked contrast to how most companys develop properties these days....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T03:35:20-07:00","id":1462638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462607#post1462607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope that W5 introduces a new Tribe like V5 introduced the Hecata, even if it isn't great it'll be interesting at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hecata arnt really a new clan they're 2 clans and 3 Bloodlines crudely stitched together as the spoopy skeleton clan, with questionable writing and a terrible discipline <br /> That said maybe bringing back the middle brother could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T03:40:25-07:00","id":1462639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462629#post1462629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who weren't interested in metaplot agnoticism because they didn't advance the setting didn't buy the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any real support for this, esp. for WtA?<br /> <br /> There's actually a lot of setting advancement in W20 even though it doesn't use metaplot. The Umbra book adds a bunch of spirits to cover new things over the last 20 years (there's a whole host of Internet spirits now), Rage Across the World added a whole new minor group of Garou, BotW20 updated Pentex for the 21st century, etc.<br /> <br /> There's quite a lot there for fans of the WtA metaplot even if not enough to have them ready to throw money at ever W20 book. While I've certainly heard people say that W20 didn't pique their interest, I've never heard anyone say it &quot;drove them off,&quot; or anything I'd consider equally empathic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People who hated V5 changes disliked the books because they changed things. </div> </div> </div>Say it with me now:<br /> <br /> &quot;People who didn't like the V5 changes dislike the books because of how the changes were implemented.&quot; Disliking how the changes were handled is not the same as disliking change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One is a lack of interest and the other is anger over changes. </div> </div> </div>But that's exactly my point. &quot;Drive off,&quot; implies anger, or at least something close to it, aimed at the book(s) in question due to developer/etc. choices; not simply indifference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I always thought the differences among the Garou would be the caerns that would have their own cultures and histories. </div> </div> </div>Something that's very different between VtM and WtA: The Garou are expected to have frequent travel and exchange between Septs. Each Sept is, of course, going to have it's individual quirks. However smaller Septs have to regularly go to larger Septs for any resources/etc. (ex: the spirits don't like being summoned to smaller Septs and pulling a spirit to a Caern rated below the level of Gift you want to learn will increase how much the spirit will demand in Chiminage for the trouble, meaning the Septs around weak Caerns will frequently send members to a nearby more power Caern since a few days of travel is better than a month long Umbra quest). The Septs are always connected by a web of Moonbridges that allow rapid transit. The Rank 5 Caerns can generate Moonbridges to pretty much any other Sept on Earth, and travel thousands of miles in under half an hour. This lets the forces concentrated at the largest Septs project their power over vast ranges, but requires they maintain good relations with those smaller Septs that are at the other end of those Moonbridges (hence a reason to give them access to resource).<br /> <br /> The Garou are also all... ideally... unified under one banner as the Garou Nation. As a monarchy, the Nation's status as a unifying factor veers wildly based on who's wearing the Crown, but Jonas is supposed to be a fairly competent leader that improved things considerably; enough to completely muck up the Margrave's plans to finally have the Shadow Lords usurp leadership from the Silver Fangs because he wasn't expecting Jonas to be able to pull in as much support as he did. While the Nation as it's politicking, it's still basically on par with the Camarilla but doesn't have the Anarchs, Independent Clans, Innconu, or powerful Autarkis to deal with, and their war with the Wyrm isn't entirely comparable to the Cam war with the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> While frequently overlooked for usefulness to actually playing the game, the Garou Nation and each Tribe has the power to call large area, or even global, gatherings of members for issues that necessitate such. <br /> <br /> All of which is to highlight how much members of the Tribes aren't separated for their fellow members geographically enough to develop truly unique local variations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rage Across Russia did a good job with the Get of Fenris for example because in Russia they were known not as a bunch of bloodthirsty berserkers but loyal honorable soldiers who were significantly more trustworthy than the Silver Fangs they served. </div> </div> </div>As far as pretty much all of the Fenrir are concerned, that's how they should be seen.<br /> <br /> Russia is also a strange case because of the Shadow Curtain that actually cut off Russia's Garou from the Nation's traditional methods of enforcing cultural norms for almost a century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T03:46:51-07:00","id":1462640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462639#post1462639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Say it with me now:<br /> <br /> &quot;People who didn't like the V5 changes dislike the books because of how the changes were implemented.&quot; Disliking how the changes were handled is not the same as disliking change.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>100% true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T05:58:59-07:00","id":1462643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462640#post1462640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 100% true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but no suggested that disliking the changes made is the same as disliking change. The ones I like will be 