=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ?<br /> <br /> &quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">People who hated V5 changes disliked the books because they changed things.</span></i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies, I said it poorly as I believe it was the specific changes they hated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T10:18:01-07:00","id":1462667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462634#post1462634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If really a majority wants updates to the setting is disputable</div> </div> </div> </div>You may be right, although I find it not only unlikely, but also probable that there are polls, surveys and statistical analysis on how much interest the public have on the Metaplot advancing.<br /> <br /> But some changes don't need a statistical significance to be valid and necessary. If a significant number of Native Americans feel that a tribe shouldn't be named after the Wendigo, and this isn't disputed among Native Americans, then the non-Native players have to accept that this is a change that need to be done. Or they'll be just wanting the right to be racist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T12:12:47-07:00","id":1462691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462667#post1462667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may be right, although I find it not only unlikely, but also probable that there are polls, surveys and statistical analysis on how much interest the public have on the Metaplot advancing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be right. But even the means they use to communicate their doing, might lead to certain directions or groups of players being more represented than others.<br /> <br /> I for example have a FB account, but do not use FB at all. I find it inherently disrespectful of legitimate privacy concerns when companies do their customer service, fan support and the like via FB. Same goes for Discord, and their Terms of use, which has clauses I just can't get on board with....<br /> <br /> Surveys that are spread amongst for example LARPers in BNS run games will attract totally different results, then surveys that reach gamers at large conventions like GenCon, or smaller Conventions in Europe, then for example the OPP forums or other game message boards in different countries and so on....<br /> <br /> Like I said about the BNS version of WtA. It caters to their perceived needs for a game system and setting. This isn't necessarily a bad thing, but it isn't the game I want to play/run either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462667#post1462667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But some changes don't need a statistical significance to be valid and necessary. If a significant number of Native Americans feel that a tribe shouldn't be named after the Wendigo, and this isn't disputed among Native Americans, then the non-Native players have to accept that this is a change that need to be done. Or they'll be just wanting the right to be racist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does the opposition to the name stem from? I mean, what is the reason the name is not acceptable to them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T12:55:59-07:00","id":1462696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462691#post1462691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does the opposition to the name stem from? I mean, what is the reason the name is not acceptable to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically because in its appropriation of the myth without consulting the peoples they belong to, <a href=\"https://www.backstoryradio.org/blog/the-mythology-and-misrepresentation-of-the-windigo/\" target=\"_blank\">White Wolf got it all wrong and added incorrect over-simplified assumptions about the myth to incorrect over-simplified assumptions about native cultures</a>.<br /> <br /> You can do a quick search with terms as <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=why%20wendigo%20is%20a%20bad%20name%20for%20a%20tribe%3F\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;why Wendigo is a bad name for a tribe&quot;</a> and you'll find plenty of interesting materials that will explain the problems with this specific stance of cultural appropriation without throwing the term in your face.<br /> <br /> No one back them consulted with Algonquian natives or even descendants to know if their use of the term was sensible in any way, they just throw in a <b>white</b> pop culture interpretation and called a day. Now you want the natives to <i>explain themselves</i> if they find it obtuse!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T13:05:23-07:00","id":1462697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462638#post1462638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Hecata arnt really a new clan they're 2 clans and 3 Bloodlines crudely stitched together as the spoopy skeleton clan, with questionable writing and a terrible discipline<br /> That said maybe bringing back the middle brother could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting is rather adamant on the principle of &quot;If Middle Brother comes back, so does the physical manifestation of the Eater of Souls&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T13:14:17-07:00","id":1462700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462691#post1462691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does the opposition to the name stem from? I mean, what is the reason the name is not acceptable to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>It comes from the Algonquin and Great Lakes peoples. You know the people for whom it's part of their actual spiritual beliefs and mythology.<br /> <br /> And the reason it's not acceptable for them, is that one of the two major sources of Native American representation in the game (and the other name isn't much better) have themselves actively serving the embodiment of evil in their culture. Having the Tribe and patron spirit of it be the Wendigo is as huge as a cultural misunderstanding as having the main Christian group in a setting being actively engage in demonic infernalism in the direct service to Satan and rejection of Jesus, while professing to honestly believe they're good Christians and the authors touting their diverse positive representation of Christianity in their work.<br /> <br /> I mean, just Google &quot;why is using the word wendigo racist&quot; and you're going to find a lot of answers from actual members of the groups in question. And it's not &quot;if&quot; but &quot;why,&quot; because they've been actively affirming that consider it overtly offensive to see how mainstream culture has twisted their spiritual beliefs for decades.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T14:27:34-07:00","id":1462712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462696#post1462696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one back them consulted with Algonquian natives or even descendants to know if their use of the term was sensible in any way, they just throw in a <b>white</b> pop culture interpretation and called a day. Now you want the natives to <i>explain themselves</i> if they find it obtuse!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I think if someone is offended, but can't really explain why, it is hard to foster understanding for their situation...<br /> <br /> <br /> And, I get that the Wendigo, meant something different in the various indigenous cultures from whom word originated from. But to what extend does one make an effort to keep the meaning of the word from changing..?<br /> Media that reach a lot of people have always shaped the general understanding of what a word means or what a thing is. Werewolves today are also removed from what they were in legends prior to 1900, due to horror films and stories. Same goes for... let's say... nordic and greek gods.<br /> <br /> I find it difficult and kind of a retroactive clean-washing if inappropriate elements like that are not addressed out of character but simply changed in books, or other media.<br /> <br /> In Germany a huge number of people like to believe native Americans to be, like they are described in the books from an author named Karl May (1842 - 1912). He was also possibly a con artist, didn't probably know anything about native Americans and might have lost touch with reality, by believing that he and his books protagonist/narrator 'Old Shatterhand', bloodbrother to the chieftain of the Apaches tribe, was in fact he himself - something his publishers were eager to push in letters to fans.<br /> His works have been made into stage shows, movies and a lot of other media.<br /> So, is it culturally inappropriate for German kids to wear costumes based on these characters? From the standpoint of a native American, possibly, but these characters are the idols of several generations, well from my grandfather's to mine, probably.<br /> <br /> The question is, at what point has a situation changed to such a degree that something has become something else within the language?<br /> And, with media spreading over the internet, this might be even more difficult to answer, since local constraints aren't really a factor anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, if the authors/IP owners aim for the garou to adopt another name for the tribe, today, possibly the tribe even gathering in a grant moot and demanding that they from now on refer to themselves by a different name, then okay, why not. If there is a sidebar explaining, that the Wendigo of myth is different to what the garou tribe was and that the IP owners believe that they should not contribute to contaminate that perception with their pop culture contribution, even better.<br /> A retcon, that the tribe was always some other named tribe, however, is something I find half-hearted, cowardly and neither educational to the readers everywhere, nor owning past deeds now deemed a mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T14:38:58-07:00","id":1462715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462700#post1462700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It comes from the Algonquin and Great Lakes peoples. You know the people for whom it's part of their actual spiritual beliefs and mythology.<br /> <br /> And the reason it's not acceptable for them, is that one of the two major sources of Native American representation in the game (and the other name isn't much better) have themselves actively serving the embodiment of evil in their culture. Having the Tribe and patron spirit of it be the Wendigo is as huge as a cultural misunderstanding as having the main Christian group in a setting being actively engage in demonic infernalism in the direct service to Satan and rejection of Jesus, while professing to honestly believe they're good Christians and the authors touting their diverse positive representation of Christianity in their work.<br /> <br /> I mean, just Google &quot;why is using the word wendigo racist&quot; and you're going to find a lot of answers from actual members of the groups in question. And it's not &quot;if&quot; but &quot;why,&quot; because they've been actively affirming that consider it overtly offensive to see how mainstream culture has twisted their spiritual beliefs for decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the explanation. It is what I gathered from the link <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> posted, too.<br /> <br /> I guess the authors didn't really face that topic, unlike the fact that Fenris role in the original myth and the WtA background kind of don't fit, which 1st Edition solved with &quot;The humans didn't interpret what happened correctly, so their myths are based on misconceptions&quot;, iirc. Which is not necessarily a rewarding thing to read, if you are following a religion that is based on the Norse gods, I imagine.<br /> <br /> Ok, I can see, that it is a difficult topic, and why there are people to advocate a change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T15:02:05-07:00","id":1462717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462712#post1462712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A retcon, that the tribe was always some other named tribe, however, is something I find half-hearted, cowardly and neither educational to the readers everywhere, nor owning past deeds now deemed a mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone here said it should be retconned and I do agree that it shouldn't. It should be faced directly as the mistake it was, admit to it and woven in the fabric of the setting as such. And I'm happy to see you understood from the link, I didn't explained more precisely because I thought that link was particularly informative on the matter.<br /> <br /> So yeah, as a pantheist with a belief in the divinity of mythology I do find the Get of Fenris <i>extremely</i> badly named and that's actually a common theme among the Tribal Totems. But at least &quot;Norse mythology&quot; do not suffer from this in the same dept and consistency of Algonquian (it is still quite bad, tho).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T15:30:46-07:00","id":1462721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462700#post1462700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It comes from the Algonquin and Great Lakes peoples. You know the people for whom it's part of their actual spiritual beliefs and mythology.<br /> <br /> And the reason it's not acceptable for them, is that one of the two major sources of Native American representation in the game (and the other name isn't much better) have themselves actively serving the embodiment of evil in their culture. Having the Tribe and patron spirit of it be the Wendigo is as huge as a cultural misunderstanding as having the main Christian group in a setting being actively engage in demonic infernalism in the direct service to Satan and rejection of Jesus, while professing to honestly believe they're good Christians and the authors touting their diverse positive representation of Christianity in their work.<br /> <br /> I mean, just Google &quot;why is using the word wendigo racist&quot; and you're going to find a lot of answers from actual members of the groups in question. And it's not &quot;if&quot; but &quot;why,&quot; because they've been actively affirming that consider it overtly offensive to see how mainstream culture has twisted their spiritual beliefs for decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>All very true.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I assume every Garou tribe should be a figure of terror and horror to humans. The Wendigo should be loathed just like the Uketena with all the other Garou tribes having names similarly repellent to humans. However, that's STILL appropriation and if it infuriates the people involved (which it does), then it should be absolutely changed.<br /> <br /> It's not even hard: Winter's Claws","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-04-2021, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T15:44:14-07:00","id":1462723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462721#post1462721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, that's STILL appropriation and if it infuriates the people involved (which it does), then it should be absolutely changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not even just that. The problem is that the association of the Wendigo with werewolves and similar creatures is, by itself, already an old white misconception that was repeated <i>ad nauseam</i>. The original myth takes the form of a tall person, just that, and represents a greedy and amoral person, not just any cannibal. So it is quite a different thing, not exactly THE devil, but it is far more a demonic figure than a beast, in both shape and behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T16:14:14-07:00","id":1462729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462723#post1462723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not even just that. The problem is that the association of the Wendigo with werewolves and similar creatures is, by itself, already an old white misconception that was repeated <i>ad nauseam</i>. The original myth takes the form of a tall person, just that, and represents a greedy and amoral person, not just any cannibal. So it is quite a different thing, not exactly THE devil, but it is far more a demonic figure than a beast, in both shape and behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, WTA is a huge amount of missteps trying to do the right thing.<br /> <br /> Like I said with Evan Heals the Past. Evan wouldn't be a terrible Child of Gaia and his message bad if the message was, &quot;The Garou Nation must acknowledge how much evil shit the European Garou did to the Native Garou.&quot; But plenty of people took him to be, &quot;White kid appropriates culture and says the Natives have to get over hating the 500 years of oppression.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is why I suspect we'll never see him again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-04-2021, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T16:43:08-07:00","id":1462733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462729#post1462729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I suspect we'll never see him again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think Evan could work fine as a Wendigo, even now, for another reason.<br /> <br /> He could be used to exemplify appropriation. He could rely his tribes concerns and be heard, <i>and the game point out that the others are talking perfectly fine, but they white men only pay attention to the white boy</i>.<br /> <br /> So we could have an Evan that isn't all that more wise and is still learning with his ancestors' people, but highlights how full of bullshit the European Garou are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T16:55:09-07:00","id":1462735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462729#post1462729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, WTA is a huge amount of missteps trying to do the right thing.<br /> <br /> Like I said with Evan Heals the Past. Evan wouldn't be a terrible Child of Gaia and his message bad if the message was, &quot;The Garou Nation must acknowledge how much evil shit the European Garou did to the Native Garou.&quot; But plenty of people took him to be, &quot;White kid appropriates culture and says the Natives have to get over hating the 500 years of oppression.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is why I suspect we'll never see him again.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, that people might have taken him as &quot;white kid&quot;, but while it is disputed in the game world, it isn't disputed that he had ancestry, that links him to the native Americans who within the game world are tied to the Wendigo tribe. Also, Ancestors Background, iirc.<br /> <br /> As a child of Gaia, Evan would have been one of many and pointless.<br /> The real point about Evan should have been to explore how a partly isolationist society, like the Wendigo are in part described as, deals with the mixed-heritage-child-of-a-mixed-heritage-child-of-a-mixed-heritage-child they would really like to forget exists. And of course, like John Oliver's Last Week Tonight stated about systematic racism, it is hard to forgive, when the oppressors aren't willing to pay reparations for what they did.<br /> <br /> White Wolf could have gone and be more bold. Make Karin Jarlsdottir a person with three out of four grandparents being afro-american. Because the Get of Fenris are heritage tied and would rather ignore away her then.<br /> <br /> It is a theme of integration into a society, someone who is perceived as not being part of that group, and what changes of the person to fit into society are necessary and what changes the society might have to make to accommodate these &quot;strays&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T21:34:48-07:00","id":1462758,"title":"","content":"All in all I think there is some form of divide between the 4th/20th Anniversary Editions and the 5th Edition(s). I see many old fans loving, reveling in and immersing themselves in the materials of 4th edition games, not only because they are more compendium like, but are of nostalgic value and have care to be so, focusing more on bringing as much options as they can, revising all of it, and give it a complete experience and possibility. So they acted like a gathering, polishing, some advances to better settle new possibilities based on what 3rd editions were doing. So you get all Clans, all Bloodlines, all Tribes, all Gifts, etc.. And we are still getting books for those editions, W20 is getting Apocalyptic Record, and seems like a confluence of all of W20's might.<br /> <br /> So I see this way, the fifth editions are about a more tabula rasa approach, while fourth editions were tabula repleta (full plate let's say), giving an approachable game by new players, less heavy in rules and lore, using the best parts (according to the creators, of course, as it is) of the setting, system and metaplot and making a renewed, strong, focused and thematic game. This of course means that what doesn't mesh together with the focused vision they have will have to be taken some way or another. V5 took a lot out, to give more strength to what it remained and/or was added. I for one have the luck of liking pretty much all of V5's choices, even then I go back to V4 to all that I wish in regards of plot and systems that V5 deliberately doesn't cast light on, or that makes vague remarks of. One is a full-pack sandwich of everything the game meddled in the previous editions, like a parade, where Becket's Diary takes vanguard, being a big love letter to all of it. The other is a new generation, fresh and light, trying new things and melting what it came before and taking all it considered more poignant and like what is trying to achieve.<br /> <br /> It might not be precisely this metaphor, but I do see as good thing, we have a full toolbox in 4th edition, and many new shiny tools in 5th edition. Some might look nasty, crude, annoying, nonsense, or useless to the users of 4th edition, but yeah, better to have the option I think. Otherwise the 4th editions would've ended up redundant or changing too much and not being able to maintain the All-Stars vibe it had. In the end, I just hope as many people as possible can enjoy the game, whatever it is, and take something they like from each new implement; and independently, just be merry with their own game and share what they cherish, and point out what they miss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T22:47:55-07:00","id":1462768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462735#post1462735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> White Wolf could have gone and be more bold. Make Karin Jarlsdottir a person with three out of four grandparents being afro-american. Because the Get of Fenris are heritage tied and would rather ignore away her then.<br /> <br /> It is a theme of integration into a society, someone who is perceived as not being part of that group, and what changes of the person to fit into society are necessary and what changes the society might have to make to accommodate these &quot;strays&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Karin Jarlsdottir didn't come onto the scene until Revised, though, which is a bit of a different case. The tribebook had fully committed to the course of &quot;the rest of the Get kill the Swords of Heimdall for being racist tools&quot; likely from the earliest stages of pre-planning, along with washing away most of the terrible bits of their earlier tribebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T22:57:45-07:00","id":1462769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462758#post1462758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All in all I think there is some form of divide between the 4th/20th Anniversary Editions and the 5th Edition(s). I see many old fans loving, reveling in and immersing themselves in the materials of 4th edition games, not only because they are more compendium like, but are of nostalgic value and have care to be so, focusing more on bringing as much options as they can, revising all of it, and give it a complete experience and possibility. So they acted like a gathering, polishing, some advances to better settle new possibilities based on what 3rd editions were doing. So you get all Clans, all Bloodlines, all Tribes, all Gifts, etc.. And we are still getting books for those editions, W20 is getting Apocalyptic Record, and seems like a confluence of all of W20's might.<br /> <br /> So I see this way, the fifth editions are about a more tabula rasa approach, while fourth editions were tabula repleta (full plate let's say), giving an approachable game by new players, less heavy in rules and lore, using the best parts (according to the creators, of course, as it is) of the setting, system and metaplot and making a renewed, strong, focused and thematic game. This of course means that what doesn't mesh together with the focused vision they have will have to be taken some way or another. V5 took a lot out, to give more strength to what it remained and/or was added. I for one have the luck of liking pretty much all of V5's choices, even then I go back to V4 to all that I wish in regards of plot and systems that V5 deliberately doesn't cast light on, or that makes vague remarks of. One is a full-pack sandwich of everything the game meddled in the previous editions, like a parade, where Becket's Diary takes vanguard, being a big love letter to all of it. The other is a new generation, fresh and light, trying new things and melting what it came before and taking all it considered more poignant and like what is trying to achieve.<br /> <br /> It might not be precisely this metaphor, but I do see as good thing, we have a full toolbox in 4th edition, and many new shiny tools in 5th edition. Some might look nasty, crude, annoying, nonsense, or useless to the users of 4th edition, but yeah, better to have the option I think. Otherwise the 4th editions would've ended up redundant or changing too much and not being able to maintain the All-Stars vibe it had. In the end, I just hope as many people as possible can enjoy the game, whatever it is, and take something they like from each new implement; and independently, just be merry with their own game and share what they cherish, and point out what they miss.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think V5 suffers the same way VtR 1st Ed suffered by simultaneously trying a whole bunch of new things but having to tie them back to older material so that it comes across as half-arsed; but V5 even moreso as it was marketed as a direct continuation of the lore of the previous editions whereas VtR 1st Ed was only using terms and concepts as a way of enticing old players to make the leap. There are obvious strains in V5 where you can see they were trying to make something entirely new but having already tied themselves to being a continuation of VtM they weren't able to fully commit to it. The amount of effort V5 had to go to to fold and spindle the old sects into new creatures entirely really held it back from finding its feet as its own game and I'm kinda hoping W5 is envisaged as a 'reimagining' of WtA with no ties to previous lore or mangling of themes and lore in order to turn one thing into another.<br /> <br /> If nothing else it would make for way less arguments online, and if we don't like it there are dozens of new W20 books every few months on Storytellers Vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 10-05-2021, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T23:16:43-07:00","id":1462770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462768#post1462768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Karin Jarlsdottir didn't come onto the scene until Revised, though, which is a bit of a different case. The tribebook had fully committed to the course of &quot;the rest of the Get kill the Swords of Heimdall for being racist tools&quot; likely from the earliest stages of pre-planning, along with washing away most of the terrible bits of their earlier tribebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was motivated by out of universe concerns obviously (Ethan Skemp said that RL gamers were using them to bring their white supremacist bullshit to LARPS as &quot;just roleplaying my character&quot;) and thus a very good decision, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Nip that shit in the bud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T01:30:39-07:00","id":1462779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462770#post1462770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was motivated by out of universe concerns obviously (Ethan Skemp said that RL gamers were using them to bring their white supremacist bullshit to LARPS as &quot;just roleplaying my character&quot;) and thus a very good decision, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Nip that shit in the bud.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see, that LARP games had a problem with the situation and surely changing the tribe's setup was a quick way to deal with this issue.<br /> Using LARPs as a means of teaching them the errors of their ways would have been another, but more exhausting way on the part of the individual ST teams per LARP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T01:41:30-07:00","id":1462780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462779#post1462779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see, that LARP games had a problem with the situation and surely changing the tribe's setup was a quick way to deal with this issue.<br /> Using LARPs as a means of teaching them the errors of their ways would have been another, but more exhausting way on the part of the individual ST teams per LARP.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a good friend of mine said, &quot;It's exhausting trying to teach bigots and they are ultimately are the people who have to decide whether they want to change.&quot;<br /> <br /> Besides, LARPs are meant to be escapist entertainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T02:02:54-07:00","id":1462781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462779#post1462779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see, that LARP games had a problem with the situation and surely changing the tribe's setup was a quick way to deal with this issue.<br /> Using LARPs as a means of teaching them the errors of their ways would have been another, but more exhausting way on the part of the individual ST teams per LARP.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From my experience, LARP STs have a full time job managing/eradicating creepers, molesters and predators without having to educated Nazis into the bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T02:15:34-07:00","id":1462784,"title":"","content":"Also, it wasn't just a problem in LARPs, it's just a lot more visible in the larger LARP communities than it is in all the small TT groups