ikes... I probably wouldn't want play LARPs in the US, when the STs have such playerbases... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In small TT groups one usually has a better handle on with whom one plays...</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many-many amazing LARPs with wonderful groups of friends. There's also always that one guy who thinks its a singles bar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T12:12:27-07:00","id":1462821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462816#post1462816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are many-many amazing LARPs with wonderful groups of friends. There's also always that one guy who thinks its a singles bar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Met my wife at a WtA LARP, so......<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T14:25:22-07:00","id":1462838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462821#post1462821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Met my wife at a WtA LARP, so......<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference, trust me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T16:52:55-07:00","id":1462845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462721#post1462721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I assume every Garou tribe should be a figure of terror and horror to humans. The Wendigo should be loathed just like the Uketena with all the other Garou tribes having names similarly repellent to humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Circling back to this because I kinda forgot about it:<br /> <br /> This makes no sense.<br /> <br /> 1) Humans aren't supposed to know the Tribes even exist. There's no point in them being scary to humans because humans are never supposed to learn enough to be scared. If the local gangs react to &quot;Bone Gnawer&quot; like small time Gotham crooks react to &quot;Batman&quot; then the Gnawers have severely fucked up.<br /> <br /> 2) These are names the Tribes use as self-identifiers. Why would the Garou call themselves evil things for terms they use to identify themselves to other Garou?<br /> <br /> 3) The Garou (mostly) maintain close ties to human ethnic/cultural groups. How are they supposed to use sub-cultures to carve out places for their human kin in human society while actively taking on the guises of things those human kin were raised to think are evil? This is one of the biggest problems with the Wendigo, Uktena, and Get of Fenris. How are the Garou via their human kin supposed to have good relations with these associated human cultures while using these names? &quot;Hi, I'm a recreation-Norse pagan who's family worships the great wolf Fenris, wanna hang out?&quot; doesn't work for people that see themselves as the good guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T17:28:14-07:00","id":1462846,"title":"","content":"I suspect ferris was chosen due to being the most famous norse wolf and they didn't think it through. A gm I knew considered renaming them after odins wolves and re-envisioning the allfather as an ally of gaia or possible a name for one of the incarna.<br /> Then again I never really considered tribes/kinfolk a direct representation of the ethnic group they're attached too. More a weird sub-culture hidden in the population. I doubt many of my home village would find much kinship with either the fianna or the dancers, despite jokes from my friends about me being dunscirn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T17:44:38-07:00","id":1462847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462845#post1462845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Circling back to this because I kinda forgot about it:<br /> <br /> This makes no sense.<br /> <br /> 1) Humans aren't supposed to know the Tribes even exist. There's no point in them being scary to humans because humans are never supposed to learn enough to be scared. If the local gangs react to &quot;Bone Gnawer&quot; like small time Gotham crooks react to &quot;Batman&quot; then the Gnawers have severely fucked up.<br /> <br /> 2) These are names the Tribes use as self-identifiers. Why would the Garou call themselves evil things for terms they use to identify themselves to other Garou?<br /> <br /> 3) The Garou (mostly) maintain close ties to human ethnic/cultural groups. How are they supposed to use sub-cultures to carve out places for their human kin in human society while actively taking on the guises of things those human kin were raised to think are evil? .</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I think that it's a cool bit of world-building that words that vampires, werewolves, and so on use for themselves have trickled down to humans and became the name of horrible monsters.<br /> <br /> In the non-cultural appropriating world where it was possible/good to use it (which is not this world), the Wendigo tribe would have inspired many legends of horrible Satanic monsters because that's what Garou are to humans.<br /> <br /> But it's a moot point for the above reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is one of the biggest problems with the Wendigo, Uktena, and Get of Fenris. How are the Garou via their human kin supposed to have good relations with these associated human cultures while using these names? &quot;Hi, I'm a recreation-Norse pagan who's family worships the great wolf Fenris, wanna hang out?&quot; doesn't work for people that see themselves as the good guys </div> </div> </div>I very much prefer the interpretation put in books like OUTCASTS and others that make it clear humans LOATHE the Garou instinctively and that any human in the presence of one with even modicum of rage will be pissing themselves out of fear. Garou do NOT have good relations with Homids and never can. They reek of serial killer and danger.<br /> <br /> Which is part of why they are eternally lonely and tortured. *brood angst Harano*<br /> <br /> I mean, your Get of Fenris guy is going to probably murder an entire village of Vikings for no reason other than they hate Odin.<br /> <br /> I know plenty of people DON'T like this interpretation of Garou but I admit I prefer the more tragic antihero version of Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-05-2021, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T18:51:31-07:00","id":1462849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462847#post1462847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I think that it's a cool bit of world-building that words that vampires, werewolves, and so on use for themselves have trickled down to humans and became the name of horrible monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that it's in direct contradiction to all the world-building to justify why 99.99% of humans don't know the truth of the WoD that they live in.<br /> <br /> Humans don't need to use the names the playable splats use to name themselves to come up with names for monsters to be scared of... we do that just fine on our own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Satanic monsters because that's what Garou are to humans. </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, they'd inspire Satanic imagery in people that have never heard of the idea of Satan for thousands of years. That even applies to Europeans and western Asians btw, you know, where Satan mythology comes from, because Satan mythology is relatively young (esp. anything that treats Satan as a demonic entity or uses Pan inspired imagery).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, your Get of Fenris guy is going to probably murder an entire village of Vikings for no reason than they hate Odin. </div> </div> </div>Because the Fenrir hate Odin, but are completely cool with Wotan... who's the same being. All of their Camps are named to honor the Aesir (and some of their Vanir allies). It's nonsense because the 1e was tossed together with zero research (to the point of making Marvel's take on the Norse gods look respectful). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know plenty of people DON'T like this interpretation of Garou but I admit I prefer the more tragic antihero version of Garou. </div> </div> </div>Because:<br /> <br /> 1) It's an interpretation that's drastically out of place with the core WtA books (which Outcasts even acknowledges it exaggerates for the tone of its own text).<br /> <br /> 2)The Garou are tragic antiheroes without it. Driving it farther doesn't make them tragic antiheroes, it' makes them grimdark amoral assholes that kill to avoid dying of depression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T19:02:05-07:00","id":1462850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462790#post1462790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yikes... I probably wouldn't want play LARPs in the US, when the STs have such playerbases... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In small TT groups one usually has a better handle on with whom one plays...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I'm not from the US that was referencing LARP I've been a part of in NZ, Australia, UK, Sweden, Norway and Denmark. Though I think we've all heard the various horror stories from US LARPs as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 10-05-2021, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T19:07:19-07:00","id":1462851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yes, they'd inspire Satanic imagery in people that have never heard of the idea of Satan for thousands of years. That even applies to Europeans and western Asians btw, you know, where Satan mythology comes from, because Satan mythology is relatively young (esp. anything that treats Satan as a demonic entity or uses Pan inspired imagery).</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, no, that's not what I meant at all.<br /> <br /> Mythological Werewolves=bad.<br /> <br /> Humans have heard of werewolves because in-universe, humans know Garou exist. They didn't come up with the werewolf legend independently.<br /> <br /> Mythological Wendigo=bad.<br /> <br /> Native Americans use the word Wendigo to describe Garou in-universe because the Wendigo tribe would be terrifying and horrible to them because werewolves=bad. They were subject to the Impergium after all.<br /> <br /> It's just horribly reductive and culturally appropriative out of universe. The Wendigo wouldn't name themselves Wendigo after the monster, they would be the monster that inspired the Wendigo. I use Satanic imagery because you did to make a comparison of how nasty and awful teh Wendigo is in their mythology.<br /> <br /> Do you see what I mean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462849#post1462849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because:<br /> <br /> 1) It's an interpretation that's drastically out of place with the core WtA books (which Outcasts even acknowledges it exaggerates for the tone of its own text).<br /> <br /> 2)The Garou are tragic antiheroes without it. Driving it farther doesn't make them tragic antiheroes, it' makes them grimdark amoral assholes that kill to avoid dying of depression.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/sWsCp1p.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I mean, it's not actually an exaggeration that one of the major themes of Werewolf: The Apocalypse is that they can't deal with humans on a non-predatory level very well and that's the primary problem they have in dealing with things like Pentex and the Weaver/Wyrm in the modern world. Garou are very good at clawing things but the fact that they instinctively scare regular humans is a important part of their subtext.<br /> <br /> You can certainly go overboard with it but I always felt that was why Kinfolk were 100% necessary. They're needed as the mediums between Garou and humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-05-2021, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T19:57:40-07:00","id":1462854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462851#post1462851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mythological Werewolves=bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mythological werewolves are complicated as humans have a very wide range of myths about them, and not all of them are bad (not necessarily good though).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humans have heard of werewolves because in-universe, humans know Garou exist. They didn't come up with the werewolf legend independently. </div> </div> </div>Humans don't know Garou exist. Most WoD humans think it's just stories and myth that have some normal explanation that older human culture didn't have the tools/knowledge to understand and used stories to explain. This isn't the CofD where humans subconsciously know the supernatural exists, but subconsciously also repress that out of a survival drive.<br /> <br /> Human werewolf mythology in the WoD is a mish-mash of Garou and other Fera, Protean using vampires, animal shifters among the mages and changelings, bygones and other non-player supernaturals, human hoaxes, human misunderstanding of real world phenomenon, human misunderstanding of other cultures, and the giant blender of time. Yes they didn't come up with it independently, but it's still exceedingly divorced from the &quot;truth.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Native Americans use the word Wendigo to describe Garou in-universe because the Wendigo tribe would be terrifying and horrible to them because werewolves=bad. They were subject to the Impergium after all. </div> </div> </div>Did you even bother looking at some of the links about this? The conflation of wendigo mythology and werewolves is European inspired make-believe. The original myths are of a gaunt or skeletal human. Why would you look at a giant raging ball of freny and claws and call it a gaunt human?<br /> <br /> This sort of logic is entirely why people need to be more careful about using stuff from cultures they're not part of. &quot;X is bad, Y is bad, so obviously it's OK to treat X = Y,&quot; is bad logic.<br /> <br /> Dragons are bad, poltergeists are bad, so clearly a German, upon seeing a dragon, would call it a poltergeist, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's just horribly reductive and culturally appropriative out of universe. </div> </div> </div>It's that in-universe too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Wendigo wouldn't name themselves Wendigo after the monster, they would be the monster that inspired the Wendigo. </div> </div> </div>Again, humans aren't supposed to know the names of the Tribes, so this short of linguistic filtering shouldn't happen.<br /> <br /> On top of that, it means the Tribes need names that make sense to the monsters in question. Werewolves have no reason to inspire the wendigo legends as they exist. It would also mean that most of the Tribes would be, &quot;the local language's word for werewolves or evil shapeshifters.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meme that doesn't work for your point </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is. Sorry horribly inaccurate to mythology Thor, you're not the smart one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, it's not actually an exaggeration... </div> </div> </div>The Outcasts extreme take is. The Garou aren't lonely and broody and tortured, because they're part of a large affirming community. Ronin are because they rejected or got rejected by that community.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...one of the major themes of Werewolf: The Apocalypse is that they can't deal with humans on a non-predatory level very well... </div> </div> </div>That's more of a conflict than a theme. Isolation from humanity isn't a theme of WtA... because the Garou can operate around humans if they want. A lot of them don't want to. The alienation of Garou society from human societies is a central conflict of the game because the Garou isolating themselves into their own smaller culture with their select kin families has left them ill-equipped to fight the war they're in on the terms the war needs to be fought on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T20:04:47-07:00","id":1462856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462851#post1462851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it's not actually an exaggeration that one of the major themes of Werewolf: The Apocalypse is that they can't deal with humans on a non-predatory level very well and that's the primary problem they have in dealing with things like Pentex and the Weaver/Wyrm in the modern world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not even remotely insurmountable unless you have really high Rage, which is kind of rare. The main reason that they can't deal with modern problems is that they don't believe that they require modern solutions. This means that you have to toe the line if you want any support from a sept or from spirits, because without Honor Renown, you can't go very far in Rank, and Honor Renown requires you to bite your tongue around elders ordering you to an effective suicide mission by not adjusting to the situation. At the very least, this means that Ahroun and Philodox are going to have to develop some really impressive social skills if they want a freer hand.<br /> <br /> But again, that is not even remotely impossible. Some tribes technically even encourage it in their culture; Shadow Lords practically require it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Garou are very good at clawing things but the fact that they instinctively scare regular humans is a important part of their subtext.<br /> <br /> You can certainly go overboard with it but I always felt that was why Kinfolk were 100% necessary. They're needed as the mediums between Garou and humans. </div> </div> </div>Kinfolk are more about long-term, multi-generational establishment of a presence in human society or among wolves in an area. Garou tend to handle gigs and drifting just fine, sometimes even if they do have very high Rage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T20:19:47-07:00","id":1462859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you even bother looking at some of the links about this? The conflation of wendigo mythology and werewolves is European inspired make-believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not understanding again. No, absolutely they have nothing in common.<br /> <br /> This is in-universe NOT actual mythology.<br /> <br /> The Wendigo as a monster is known as a Wendigo in-universe because Wendigo werewolves left such a terrible impression on the culture.<br /> <br /> Just like Toreadors aren't named after bullfighters, bullfighters are presumably named after Toreador.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sort of logic is entirely why people need to be more careful about using stuff from cultures they're not part of. &quot;X is bad, Y is bad, so obviously it's OK to treat X = Y,&quot; is bad logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why I repeatedly said that it was not a comparison that makes any sense and provided numerous warnings. This is just the idea that they could have gone with the idea of hints of the REAL truth of werewolves trickling donw through mythology to the public. Possibly through Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, humans aren't supposed to know the names of the Tribes, so this short of linguistic filtering shouldn't happen.<br /> <br /> On top of that, it means the Tribes need names that make sense to the monsters in question. Werewolves have no reason to inspire the wendigo legends as they exist. It would also mean that most of the Tribes would be, &quot;the local language's word for werewolves or evil shapeshifters.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves would inspire such legends because they're a plageu on humanity that killed uncounted millions that left a psychic scare on humanity. So much so that every generation thereafter instinctively fears them to the point of temporary insanity.<br /> <br /> And yes, that's totally the way they should have done it. Garou should have a lot of clues like the Get of Fenris that they are the &quot;bad guys&quot; in mythology.<br /> <br /> I think the big issue is that it is ONLY the Native American tribes that are like this. The Black Furies should be the Eriynes or something.<br /> <br /> In any case, they absolutely should change the Wendigo and Uktena tribe names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-05-2021, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T20:38:06-07:00","id":1462862,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462849#post1462849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's nonsense because the 1e was tossed together with zero research (to the point of making Marvel's take on the Norse gods look respectful).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's extremely true. Later authors went through great efforts to justify several 1st edition nonsense decisions. The totems are the result of an understanding of mythologies around the world that made Saint Seiya look like a reasonable approach. The &quot;Garou language&quot; is a complete mess. Every tribe was a victim to this to some extent, with Fenrir being maybe the second worse. And this started to get more glaring as the books introduced more elements of the cultures those tribes were meant to represent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462851#post1462851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can certainly go overboard with it but I always felt that was why Kinfolk were 100% necessary. They're needed as the mediums between Garou and humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason Kinfolk are necessary is because someone have to handle the less war-like Garou affairs. Managing non-magical assets, getting money, building safe places and bunkers, a war-like race that also commands many human affairs from the shadows (because, y'know, they are ALSO secret masters even if less involved than Vampires and Mages) needs a lot of hands doing other things than being warriors, so better be smart with resources and focus your big balls of fur and death on the things that kinfolk can't do.<br /> <br /> What really makes kinfolk 100% necessary is Garou isolationism and aversion to modernity. And that's it. Strained relations between Garou and humans exist, but are just one thing, not a central theme. This is not a game about feeling bad for being yourself, even if it welcomes you feeling angry with the jerks that act like monsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462859#post1462859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wendigo as a monster is known as a Wendigo in-universe because Wendigo werewolves left such a terrible impression on the culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're not. That's your idea, but not the canon.<br /> <br /> The Wendigo are named like that because their totem is the Wendigo, and humans have the myth of the Wendigo <u>also</u> because of the totem.<br /> <br /> In WtA humans have no idea about the reality or internal names of splats, but they DO know spirits, because the spirits aren't and never were bound to no frigging Masquerade. Werewolves really share gods and totems with the human cultures they live around. What a Black Fury calls Pegasus is the same entity a human calls Pegasus, even if its &quot;real&quot; history isn't quite the same. But with spirits it is close.<br /> <br /> And that is the big problem with the tribes Wendigo and Get of Fenris. It can't be said that the legends were named after then because it is <u>already canonical</u> that they were named after the legends. And likewise that humans weren't inspired by the get or Little Brother, but by the actual spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T20:46:14-07:00","id":1462864,"title":"","content":"You are 100% correct. I forgot about the totem and my idea is disproven by canon. :thumbs up:<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T20:54:05-07:00","id":1462866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462859#post1462859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, absolutely they have nothing in common.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why a fiction world where werewolves inspired wendio mythology is still bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is just the idea that they could have gone with the idea of hints of the REAL truth of werewolves trickling donw through mythology to the public. Possibly through Kinfolk. </div> </div> </div>And you're skipping the dragons vs. angry ghosts comparison. The filtering you're wishing was part of the game would still need to make sense. Werewolves shouldn't be inspiring myths that have nothing to do with werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolves would inspire such legends because they're a plageu on humanity that killed uncounted millions that left a psychic scare on humanity. So much so that every generation thereafter instinctively fears them to the point of temporary insanity. </div> </div> </div>And the Delirium makes most people forget things, which makes it hard to form mythologies around events when nobody remembers what really happened and explicitly remembers it as somethin more mundane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Garou should have a lot of clues like the Get of Fenris that they are the &quot;bad guys&quot; in mythology. </div> </div> </div>Why? They've spent thousands of years (1) making sure humans don't know the truth and (2) trying to influence mythology so they're the good guys they believe they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the big issue is that it is ONLY the Native American tribes that are like this. </div> </div> </div>*looks at all the talk about the Fenrir*<br /> <br /> Uh...huh...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Black Furies should be the Eriynes or something. </div> </div> </div>The Black Furies believe their founding members were the Eriynes, like the Fenrir believe Fenris was the progenitor of their Tribe. Why do you think they're the Black <b>Furies.</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T01:03:24-07:00","id":1462878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462854#post1462854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, humans aren't supposed to know the names of the Tribes, so this short of linguistic filtering shouldn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Save from the Glass Walkers all tribe names are relatively old (yet English, for some reason).<br /> <br /> With the transition of what W20 calls &quot;kenning&quot; kinfolk to non-kenning to eventually humans the folklore did change but it didn't magically erase certain terms from the language.<br /> <br /> In addition to the fact, that the spirits might have interacted with humans more regularly in ages past, there is also the first Werewolf supplement to Vampire The Dark Ages. It states, that the tenet of the Veil was not originally part of the Litany but was introduced by the Silverfangs around 1000AD and adopted by the other tribes. The ramifications for the Pure Lands probably were to no concern to the authors...<br /> <br /> In any case, the names of the monsters, like the names of gods and other mystical figures, might have been not only fearful for the humans but also awe-inspiring. Therefore it is conceivable that the garou adopted them as self-describing terms, especially since the number of homids grew and human language became more commonly used in septs.<br /> <br /> In any case, it should be a case to case analysis per tribe...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T02:32:52-07:00","id":1462880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462878#post1462878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Save from the Glass Walkers all tribe names are relatively old (yet English, for some reason).<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are in High Tongue, we just get the translation of the concepts in english.<br /> <br /> Except for The Three Brothers....which is another reason in an increasingly long list not to use them.<br /> <br /> The Fenrir just took the local human name for their Patron and he liked it enough to let them use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T02:38:19-07:00","id":1462881,"title":"","content":"By definition callow kin don't know anything about their Garou relatives to know what the names of any of the Tribes are. That stuff you need to learn, not stuff you're born knowing, and if someone's teaching you... you'd be kenning kin.<br /> <br /> The 2e VtDA Werewolf book is drastically out of line with the rest of the game. The Veil in any other book that discusses it was introduced as part of the Concord to end the Impergium (at most as recent as 9000 years ago). While the books note that the Three Brothers were less harsh in the culling of humans, and had better relations with the humans in their lands for it (and thus far more of them are kin), the books never say that the Three Brothers didn't follow the Litany, or that keeping the Veil wasn't part of the Litany they use for as long as they've been in the Americas. This is notable since there was a chance for Younger Brother to learn about any changes as there was some contact between them and the Garou in Siberia until the rise of the Shadow Curtain.<br /> <br /> So, while the Veil was definitely not part of the original Litany, it's been around for far too long for the filtering in question to have happened.<br /> <br /> And the problem with a case to case analysis is that the only cases to bother with are Older and Younger Brother, and the Get of Fenris. The Fianna and the Black Furies are closest to being cases (Fianna just means &quot;war band&quot; but has strong ties to Irish mythology and the constant fighting in it, and the Black Furies don't have a particular disconnect between themselves and their namesakes' cultural legacy), but neither is a reference to a monster or evil entity; even if not friendly to humans either. All of the other Tribes have generic names with no specific connections to mythological monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T08:47:10-07:00","id":1462894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462878#post1462878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Save from the Glass Walkers all tribe names are relatively old (yet English, for some reason).</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't English, it is translatable. With very few exceptions we don't call the Tribes in Brazil, at least, by the names used in English-speaking countries. It makes sense, since they use descriptive names.<br /> <br /> To me they are Presas de Prata, Senhores das Sombras, Peregrinos Silencioso, Garras Vermelhas,F\u00farias Negras, Crias de Fenris, Andarilhos do Asfalto, Roedores de Ossos, Filhos de Gaia, Portadores da Luz Interior, Uivadores Brancos, Dan\u00e7arinos da Pele e Dan\u00e7arinos da Espiral Negra. The only ones untranslatable are Wendigo, Uktena and Fianna, for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> A trickling of Garou words into human myth would be conceivable, but didn't really happened in canon. Spirits aren't Garou, they are far better known by humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462880#post1462880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for The Three Brothers...</div> </div> </div> </div>And Fianna. Don't forget Fianna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T17:27:52-07:00","id":1462945,"title":"","content":"On reflection werewolf tribal naming trends are a bit of a mess. I wonder if this links back to their historical point of origin. Simpler names from earlier periods or geographical trends.<br /> It'd be interesting to comment on what their names translate into the garou language and lupus communication. The idea of tribes have a specific howl which doesn't translate over is an interesting one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-06-2021, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T20:06:45-07:00","id":1462958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462894#post1462894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Fianna. Don't forget Fianna.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that was cited as meaning &quot;war band&quot; or &quot;soldiers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T20:50:32-07:00","id":1462960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462945#post1462945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On reflection werewolf tribal naming trends are a bit of a mess. I wonder if this links back to their historical point of origin. Simpler names from earlier periods or geographical trends.<br /> It'd be interesting to comment on what their names translate into the garou language and lupus communication. The idea of tribes have a specific howl which doesn't translate over is an interesting one</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who speaks English as her second language, I think most of the werewolf tribe names work pretty well. After all, they can be adapted to different languages very easily as there is no hint that they are called that in every country. It also works in terms of the more animalistic aspects of the garou, as the names are literally just descriptors.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T21:35:04-07:00","id":1462963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462958#post1462958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that was cited as meaning &quot;war band&quot; or &quot;soldiers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But his comment was about untranslated names. It is a translatable name, but went &quot;untranslated&quot;. Everyone gets Fianna.<br /> <br /> Which, by the way, is also &quot;deer&quot; in Welsh and Scottish Gaelic. You know, the female of a stag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T22:37:23-07:00","id":1462974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462963#post1462963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But his comment was about untranslated names. It is a translatable name, but went &quot;untranslated&quot;. Everyone gets Fianna.<br /> <br /> Which, by the way, is also &quot;deer&quot; in Welsh and Scottish Gaelic. You know, the female of a stag.</div> </div> </div> </div>*writes that down for I WAS A TEENAGE WEREDEER book*<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T02:25:01-07:00","id":1462987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462963#post1462963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But his comment was about untranslated names. It is a translatable name, but went &quot;untranslated&quot;. Everyone gets Fianna.<br /> <br /> Which, by the way, is also &quot;deer&quot; in Welsh and Scottish Gaelic. You know, the female of a stag.</div> </div> </div> </div> At the risk of giving away about myself then I'd like, the Welsh for deer is carw. Gaelic/Scottish belongs to a different branch than Welsh and their isn't a direct equivalent of fianna because the word carries certain cultural connotations which don't translate over. My Welsh is mediocre but i think the closest terms would be Arwyr (heroes), marchog (knight) or grwp rhyfel (group of warriors) I'd go with marchogion ceirw or rhyfemwyr ceirw if I wanted to convey what the fianna are in Welsh but I'd probably just stick with with fianna since it's a noun anyway and the fianna have usually been written as more Irish than pan celtic<br /> Amusingly get of fenris could be translated as Plant fenris depending on how you interpret get and silver fangs is fangs arian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-07-2021, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T10:56:40-07:00","id":1463006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462987#post1462987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of giving away about myself then I'd like, the Welsh for deer is carw. Gaelic/Scottish belongs to a different branch than Welsh and their isn't a direct equivalent of fianna because the word carries certain cultural connotations which don't translate over.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was totally just using Google Translator and was indeed surprised that Welsh and Gaelic were giving the same translation. It wasn't, in any way, an indication that I believe that those translations were sufficient or adequate.<br /> <br /> As I said everyone is stuck with Fianna, the only tribe name so fixed in a single culture that it just isn't translated. The &quot;Pure&quot; Tribes and the Fenris are called by the totem's name at least, but the Fianna are just the Scottish equivalent of <i>Sentai</i>, as in &quot;I totally can translate this, but I won't because <i>kawai desu</i>&quot; (\u53ef\u611b\u3044\u3067\u3059, finally got to install kanji support in this PC).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T11:20:51-07:00","id":1463008,"title":"","content":"This reminds me how during Dark Ages I try to show how most of what we know from the Cainite Clans are iconography and name conventions from them, and how many of them were names given by outsiders. Like tell me if you are deep complex clan, with a long history and many fields, and you call yourself Theshadow, or Witch but written differently. So I try to show that the name and this rightly and neat construction of Clans and where they end and begin is almost modern, at the very least from the 14th century. Even the stereotypes were being built in the Dark Ages: Ventrue are what Hardestadt and Mithrs was, Gangrel were Arnulf, Tzimisce were Rustovitch, Toreador were all the Parisian Toreador... etc. <br /> So I imagine, especially for a society like the Garou that are built over symbols and an universal language that their name conventions really shifts. But I don't get enough of the Werewolf lore and tribes history to give anything concrete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T12:18:48-07:00","id":1463020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463006#post1463006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said everyone is stuck with Fianna, the only tribe name so fixed in a single culture that it just isn't translated. The &quot;Pure&quot; Tribes and the Fenris are called by the totem's name at least, but the Fianna are just the Scottish equivalent of <i>Sentai</i>, as in &quot;I totally can translate this, but I won't because <i>kawai desu</i>&quot; (\u53ef\u611b\u3044\u3067\u3059, finally got to install kanji support in this PC).</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't disagree with the general point, it is hard to actually translate &quot;fianna&quot; idiomatically. While it is, literally, a war-band, there are a bunch of cultural connotations attached to how they operate (fianna were made up of young nobles and aristocrats that had not yet inherited land of their own, had to operate in service to a landed individual to wage war legitimately, in some cases they had restrictions on what non-war activities they could use to make a living, probably a later invention they had a philosophic code).<br /> <br /> It's kind of like translating &quot;samurai.&quot; Just saying it means &quot;retainer&quot; isn't going to convey their whole cultural place in Japanese traditions.<br /> <br /> I think that just makes the case that it's a bad name for a Tribe (it's does way too much to make them the Irish Tribe instead of a larger Celtic Tribe) because it relies too much on such a specific cultural context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463008#post1463008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the stereotypes were being built in the Dark Ages: Ventrue are what Hardestadt and Mithrs was, Gangrel were Arnulf, Tzimisce were Rustovitch, Toreador were all the Parisian Toreador... etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtM has plenty of official material that makes the case that the Clan names were, at least in the past, not universal for most of history. The modern names are mostly the product of the post Anarch Revolt consolidation of vampire society and certain names becoming normalized for the whole Clan. We know that at least India, the Middle East, and Africa have different names for at least some of the Clans that are still used in modern nights. So this is probably the right take for VtM.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T03:21:33-07:00","id":1463080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462881#post1462881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2e VtDA Werewolf book is drastically out of line with the rest of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>In some cases, sure. But it wasn't so much the case, when it was released.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1462881#post1462881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Veil in any other book that discusses it was introduced as part of the Concord to end the Impergium (at most as recent as 9000 years ago).</div> </div> </div> </div>Really. Is there a source reference for that?<br /> <br /> <br /> And sure, all the names are translatable, possibly, and sure, we use German names for the tribes as well, except for Uktena, Wendigo, Bunyip and Fianna. Those just don't translate well. We also don't translate auspice names, although Ragabash is, iirc, an old Scottish expression. For some, we often use German pronunciation, though. Theurge for example is based on a latin word, so we don't make the English &quot;th&quot; sound, but go with a t and silent h.<br /> <br /> Thing is, we don't have High Tongue words and pronunciation provided, and so we don't use them in games, especially LARPs, short of the few parts of vocabulary in the core rules and alternative auspice names in the 1st edition tribe books.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <br /> Sure, the definition of callow kin versus kenning kin is that some know squat and other know a bit more up to everything. But there has to be a grey area, I think. Over centuries the kinfolk communities grew larger and people grew apart from their garou cousins and the septs, but they didn't magically forget about them. And since the kin communities also might identify themselves with the tribe names as names for their own communities as well.<br /> CtD's Mists or WtO's Shroud might magically alter memories and stuff to protect, but the Veil doesn't work like that. Well, it does, if the Veil is used to describe the memory alteration effects of the Delirium, but not if it is used as the general practice to keep the general human population in the dark about werewolf existence, like the Litany demands.<br /> <br /> So, if Bob does not attend the sept's festivities but used to do so as a kid, for his parents were pretty active in the community, and his brother still is, then he is callow or kenning? What about Bob's daughter Ellie, who dosn't know anything, except that her uncle is regularly meeting with some folks &quot;in the mountains&quot; and has once overheard that her uncle wants Bob to &quot;join the other Fenrir in celebration of something&quot;....<br /> <br /> It is my believe, that the names (although possibly distorted) of tribes are most likely elements of garou society that will have swept over into certain areas of human society. And might be something, that occult scholars might know, even if they know little to nothing else about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T10:31:18-07:00","id":1463112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463080#post1463080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is my believe, that the names (although possibly distorted) of tribes are most likely elements of garou society that will have swept over into certain areas of human society. And might be something, that occult scholars might know, even if they know little to nothing else about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't that this theory doesn't make sense, but simply that it isn't a thing on canon.<br /> <br /> Wendigo, Uktena, Croatan, Bunyip and Fenrir are names of spirits and canonically people know those names because of the spirits, not of the tribes. The spirits don't give a shit about any Veil and interact with humans from time to time, or even are created out of human belief, either way the legends of those creatures predate their elected tribe's naming. The setting could have been done in another way. It wasn't.<br /> <br /> So as far a canon goes, virtually no word trickled down from Garou culture to human culture, but the opposite happened a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T10:35:18-07:00","id":1463115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463112#post1463112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So as far a canon goes, virtually no word trickled down from Garou culture to human culture, but the opposite happened a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that remotely likely?<br /> <br /> It seems silly to assume they need a rule for the Veil if its never broken.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T10:45:15-07:00","id":1463118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463006#post1463006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the Fianna are just the Scottish equivalent...</div> </div> </div> </div>To be precise, the Fianna were Irish, not Scots. In the Irish mythology, the Fianna were the warriors that fought alongside Finn MacCool and the term &quot;fenian&quot; is commonly used to refer to the Irish people. Oh, and &quot;fia&quot; means &quot;deer&quot; in Irish, so I THINK &quot;fianna&quot; is the plural of &quot;fia&quot; (not sure here, because I know just a wee bit of Irish) and maybe that's why the Google Translator messed up.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img19/986/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","name":"Wolfen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T10:57:19-07:00","id":1463119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463112#post1463112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as far a canon goes, virtually no word trickled down from Garou culture to human culture, but the opposite happened a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a source for that? Because I'm pretty sure the canon says the High Tongue influenced the human languages...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img19/986/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","name":"Wolfen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T14:00:05-07:00","id":1463149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463115#post1463115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that remotely likely?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it can be argued to be a moot exchange. If it happens rarely and in a smaller scale than the Garou absorbing human culture, it wouldn't be totally unfeasible that significant bits can't be recognized.<br /> <br /> Like, some words for some monsters or myths or whatnot could have been originated among the Garou, but so long ago that not even the Garou recognize their origins as both the language in which they created the word is long dead and lost and the word itself went through several changes through time. That would make this something a trained team of linguists can find in their analysis, but is utterly irrelevant for a lay person and of little application in the game (unless you have a team of linguists involved in the plot).<br /> <br /> So it is extremely unlikely, but we have to remember that words being so perfectly mirrored aren't also something that happens. Search for etymologies of various words and you'll see some wild transformations in spelling, pronunciation, context and precise meaning before they reach their current form, and it is even worse with nouns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463119#post1463119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a source for that? Because I'm pretty sure the canon says the High Tongue influenced the human languages...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, let me express better my thought: no particular human word in any language derives directly of how the Garou name things in a manner that you can say that word &quot;x&quot; is originally from the Garou culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T15:01:51-07:00","id":1463161,"title":"","content":"The way language exchange work in WtA is also just another one of those massive clusters of trying to fix bad ideas from 1e.<br /> <br /> Like, the Garou have apparently been using the word ronin for thousands of years before it developed in Japanese culture. So the Japanese clearly got it from them. Though, of course, this is nonsense because the authors just liked the word ronin and shoved it in to a lexicon that's mostly a mashup of Gaulish, Germanic, and Romance languages with some sprinkling from nearby languages like Greek (though that's normal for Romance languages anyway).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately they never retconed that, even while pivoting strongly towards the idea that Garou High Tongue has dialects and the common modern lexicon is largely a product of the Fianna and Silver Fangs, with High Tongue loan words from other dialects that - like ronin - capture a meaning more elegantly. But the books haven't really explored other High Tongue dialects in any real detail (including Native American despite the isolation of the Three Brothers and having multiple books where discussing such matters would have been a useful bit of world building), and their existence clearly backs up the idea that Garou culture ends up borrowing from human culture (as the source for these dialectical differences is based on human divisions). But we never got any real coherent way for human culture to incorporate Garou language elements. Kin can't actually learn High Tongue (at least not without being a Kami - which is a really strange word for the authors to use - or some other supernatural that's going to set them apart from humanity too). When Garou are conversing in High Tongue, and they translate any important messages to their kin, it's going to be into the local language. Irish kinfolk in the 1000s didn't know the word ronin, they knew whatever Irish phrase their Fianna relatives translated the High Tongue word that we translate as ronin now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T01:34:28-07:00","id":1463209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463149#post1463149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, let me express better my thought: no particular human word in any language derives directly of how the Garou name things in a manner that you can say that word &quot;x&quot; is originally from the Garou culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're saying that there's no human word in any language that is EXACTLY THE SAME in the High Tongue, then I agree, because it's impossible even for the Garou to speak the High Tongue in human form. But there are many human words that do derive (as in they are etymologically derivated) from Garou words.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img19/986/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","name":"Wolfen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T08:39:00-07:00","id":1463228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463209#post1463209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there are many human words that do derive (as in they are etymologically derivated) from Garou words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you provide an example that is both canonical and relevant to this conversation? I think you're fixated in a detail that isn't really what I was talking about, but I may be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T12:02:57-07:00","id":1463246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463112#post1463112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem isn't that this theory doesn't make sense, but simply that it isn't a thing on canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there an explicit mention, that no human would ever know a tribe name?<br /> Are humans banned from Garou Lore or Lupine Lore secondary skill?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463112#post1463112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, let me express better my thought: no particular human word in any language derives directly of how the Garou name things in a manner that you can say that word &quot;x&quot; is originally from the Garou culture.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463112#post1463112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you provide an example that is both canonical and relevant to this conversation? I think you're fixated in a detail that isn't really what I was talking about, but I may be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I couldn't provide a word.<br /> But then again, Garou High Tongue isn't Tolkin's Evlish or Star Trek's Klingon, as in, we are not provided a full and complex guide to the language.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <br /> Ronin could have, as an expression, developed in Japanese and Garou language in parallel - without influencing each other. But that is highly unlikely. Also, the descriptions of the Bone Gnawers in the Dark Ages and before that indicate that they recruited their members from cast-offs and washouts of other tribes. I imagine that they themselves didn't have cast offs in numbers that made it necessary to coin a term. I think Ronins, as is, is a more modern phenomenon. So, I'd argue that garou usage of the expressions for a long time is probably false narration on some sourcebooks part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T14:17:43-07:00","id":1463253,"title":"","content":"There's a fairly massive difference between, &quot;I'm an Arcanum scholar that's studied werewolves extensively and I've begun to understand there's a global werewolf culture with subcultures that have distinct names and identities with in it,&quot; and, &quot;As a normal human being [unknowingly living in a universe called the World of Darkness], and for some reason the idea of red talons feels really wrong to me, and when I talk to people they all seem to agree, but nobody knows why exactly.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because the second one is what's actually being discussed. Where Garou language has penetrated into human culture, not whether or not the rare outsider humans that study the Garou can figure out stuff if they're lucky enough to not get caught by the Garou and killed.<br /> <br /> The problem with ronin is that we know when it became a thing in Japanese culture: the 700s and the rise of a form of feudalism. Before it's most commonly used meaning now, it meant anyone that wasn't part of that system (so a serf farmer who's farm was destroyed and became a beggar would be a ronin for no longer serving as a serf to a local lord, not just the idea of masterless samurai). The books however, to explain the presence of ronin in High Tongue, did claim that the Garou invented it first, and implied that somehow the Japanese got it from them; not some incidental parallel process.<br /> <br /> However, this reasoning as never widely applied because the authors didn't feel the need to explain the presence of English and English adjacent words in the standard High Tongue Lexicon, since the impression there is that they're only English with archaic twists and some borrow word from languages English borrows from heavily as a translation convention.<br /> <br /> So the books created the idea that Garou words have filtered into human use, but never explains how or why or how many. It also maintains that the High Tongue is incoherent to humans, and that the words we use are translations of it, not the true words used in that language. This creates an incoherent setting element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T16:09:15-07:00","id":1463259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463253#post1463253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books however, to explain the presence of ronin in High Tongue, did claim that the Garou invented it first, and implied that somehow the Japanese got it from them; not some incidental parallel process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a page reference for that?<br /> <br /> Regarding your two examples, I wasn't aware we were discussing the second. I would have gone for more in the middle approaches. &quot;Project Twilight&quot; states, the US government only knows about Uktena, Wendigo and BSD, but is not clear (to me) if this knowledge includes these names specifically.<br /> <br /> I think the Red Talons are a bad example for my statement, that with kinfolk drifting apart from their septs and making the transition for kenning to callow, possibly over a generation or two, some elements of the garou culture get integrated into human society... And that is just not the case for Red Talons, because they lack human kinfolk.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T16:16:16-07:00","id":1463263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463246#post1463246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an explicit mention, that no human would ever know a tribe name?</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said we're discussing cultural influence, not knowledge. And the lore factually presents the tribes' names as never leaking into human culture. No one named a monster, legend or whatever after some tribe, they're all names completely unknown for <i>human culture at large</i>.<br /> <br /> The examples we have of alleged influence are incoherent due to the authors not knowing or caring about etymology in any level when they gave the idea, just as a way to justify a Nation extremely isolationist using a lot of unrelated jargon cherry picked from wherever they fancied for sounding cool. It doesn't extend to names, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T23:12:35-07:00","id":1463287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463263#post1463263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said we're discussing cultural influence, not knowledge. And the lore factually presents the tribes' names as never leaking into human culture. No one named a monster, legend or whatever after some tribe, they're all names completely unknown for <i>human culture at large</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, is there a page reference for that?<br /> I mean, from the top of my head, Fenris and the Furies are part of human culture. But both were spirits or bygones at some point, so the influence didn't necessarily come from the garou alone, but it doesn't mean it didn't come from them on parts. The practice of stargazing is also known to humans, and garou mystics of that tribe influenced human mystics and vice versa. Gaia, also a spirit/god/bygone entity, known to humans - children of Gaia is a term, human groups might develop in parallel to the tribe name, but also might learn it from garou, since the tribe is classically close to humans, going so far as to invite non-kinfolk humans to their Earth Day seasonal Rite. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T13:17:53-07:00","id":1463346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463287#post1463287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, is there a page reference for that?<br /> I mean, from the top of my head, Fenris and the Furies are part of human culture. But both were spirits or bygones at some point, so the influence didn't necessarily come from the garou alone, but it doesn't mean it didn't come from them on parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quibble: Bygones as a concept don't exist in Werewolf. It doesn't touch on them, and in fact, disbelief will not prevent you from being graboid-ed by thunderwyrms, nor keep them away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The practice of stargazing is also known to humans, and garou mystics of that tribe influenced human mystics and vice versa. Gaia, also a spirit/god/bygone entity, known to humans - children of Gaia is a term, human groups might develop in parallel to the tribe name, but also might learn it from garou, since the tribe is classically close to humans, going so far as to invite non-kinfolk humans to their Earth Day seasonal Rite. </div> </div> </div>CoG approaches like that are extremely recent, and sometimes, one can't even rely on CoG rites being concepts that can actually exist in the setting (well, hello there Rite of Clouds and Rain). In this case, though, they're probably disguising the rites so thoroughly that not much of actual Garou culture is going to bleed through, because that would be a violation of The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted, and that's something that the Garou actually tend to take seriously, along with protecting caerns.<br /> <br /> Garou are also unlikely to have ever taken the advice of human mystics, because either they're low-level workers of the art that the Garou can run circles around and who they think of as very stunted and backward, or they're mages, who often don't even go along with the reality of the Garou and Fera. Note that the Garou and Fera view of the stars differs substantially from the human one, because they were visiting the Aetherial Realm for tens of thousands of years and never told any human shit about the planets that humans missed prior to the invention of powerful telescopes. It wasn't for humans, and that's the attitude that the Garou have taken, for good or for ill, with regard to their society. Any bits that get out aren't significant cultural knowledge, they're stray bits that get the Bob Schnoblin treatment, especially after humans started fitting everything into their own religions, and even more so if or when said religions started to centralize heavily and clamp down on anything that went against a central authority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T18:41:02-07:00","id":1463361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463228#post1463228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you provide an example that is both canonical and relevant to this conversation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, pretty much any time there's an overlap between the High Tongue and a human language the humans got the word from the werewolves, that's how the setting was created. &quot;Garou&quot; didn't come from the French, &quot;lupus&quot; didn't come from the Romans, &quot;Gaia&quot; didn't come from the Greeks and so on and so forth. There are literally hundreds of terms used to describe the society and the culture of the shapeshifters (not just the Garou) and these terms were not taught by humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463228#post1463228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're fixated in a detail that isn't really what I was talking about, but I may be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about the High Tongue as a whole and not some specific detail, but feel free to correct me if I'm missing your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img19/986/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","name":"Wolfen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T19:54:58-07:00","id":1463365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463361#post1463361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the High Tongue as a whole and not some specific detail, but feel free to correct me if I'm missing your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about the idea of some monster legends be the result of a Garou <b>tribe's name</b> trickling down to human culture. It seems we're not talking about the same thing at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463287#post1463287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, from the top of my head, Fenris and the Furies are part of human culture. But both were spirits or bygones at some point, so the influence didn't necessarily come from the garou alone, but it doesn't mean it didn't come from them on parts. The practice of stargazing is also known to humans, and garou mystics of that tribe influenced human mystics and vice versa. Gaia, also a spirit/god/bygone entity, known to humans - children of Gaia is a term, human groups might develop in parallel to the tribe name, but also might learn it from garou, since the tribe is classically close to humans, going so far as to invite non-kinfolk humans to their Earth Day seasonal Rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fenrir, Gaia, Wendigo, Uktena, Croatan and Bunnyip are all spirits. Humans know something about spirits for several reasons, not the least because humans also have mediums and shamans, even if far less skillful. Also because spirits don't follow the Litany and don't give a fuck to the Veil, never gave. The books make it clear that human legend about those things are stories about the spirits themselves, and not some weird memory of the werewolf tribes that they remember the name and started to associate and transform. Human legends on the Uktena are legends about the spirit, not about the tribe.<br /> <br /> Black Furies, Get of Fenris and Stargazers each argue some interconnection between their culture and human cultures around them, but there's a lot of caveats to this. The Stargazers claim that Klaital had a monastery open to everyone, but they don't claim this to be the necessary origin of monastic practices and pretty much don't care, as they put greater emphasis in the interpretation of a story and accept clashing versions as mere aspects of the truth. The Get of Fenris have completely different stories for the gods of the Eddas, but they claim this as a result of the \u00c6sir lying, not of humans interpreting their interactions with the tribe. And finally the Furies do believe Greek mythology to be derived directly from their history, but they're also one of the most disdainful of writing down their legends, so you have to take everything with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> No indication exists of human legends ever being based and named on interactions with any other tribe, at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T19:59:29-07:00","id":1463366,"title":"","content":"I mean, I personally imagine the Garou should leave an imprint on human society rather than just the Spirits themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T20:53:35-07:00","id":1463378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463366#post1463366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I personally imagine the Garou should leave an imprint on human society rather than just the Spirits themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that it makes sense, but then there are some problems from a Doylist perspective:<br /> <br /> 1- You have to account for the other splats, and then you run into the problem of how much you'll let each be the factor behind something and how it'll translate into the others. Can you answer this without pissing off some players more than it's worth?<br /> <br /> 2- You have to take into account the impact of such interpretations on irl cultures. The Wendigo are in the current place, but the first big crisis was actually the Get of Fenris, and a lot of players still don't take well the whole thing. Then Chechnya remembers us what ignoring real causes to invent fictional ones can look like.<br /> <br /> 3- You'll have a lot of work avoiding stupidity. Again, look at the High Tongue for an example of a mess, as few players I know really buy the idea that a salad of cool words is actually derived from the same proto-language and werewolves from far and wide use them in the same way for tradition.<br /> <br /> Not that it isn't a valid undertaking, just expressing that making it into actual canonical material is hard. And here we have the added problem of the setting being already running, so thinker with it without overruling previous canon doesn't makes things easier.<br /> <br /> Personally I like how Forsaken dealt with the Tongue aspect, keeping to faux-Summer instead of grabbing random worlds all around the place. But it is only one possible take and have its obvious limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T23:13:56-07:00","id":1463384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463365#post1463365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the idea of some monster legends be the result of a Garou <b>tribe's name</b> trickling down to human culture. It seems we're not talking about the same thing at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Sorry. I was thinking in more general terms of Garou vocabulary entering the human languages - not just informing some monster legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T03:28:37-07:00","id":1463408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463365#post1463365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the idea of some monster legends be the result of a Garou <b>tribe's name</b> trickling down to human culture. It seems we're not talking about the same thing at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be honest, after reading quotes like these...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463365#post1463365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as far a canon goes, virtually no word trickled down from Garou culture to human culture, but the opposite happened a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463365#post1463365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some words for some monsters or myths or whatnot could have been originated among the Garou</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463365#post1463365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no particular human word in any language derives directly of how the Garou name things</div> </div> </div> </div>...you don't come across as talking <b>only</b> about some Tribes' names. But OK, since you don't question my point that there are lots of Garou terms that influenced the human culture, I'll continue from that and just narrow it to the Tribes that are named after a supernatural entity: Black Furies, Children of Gaia, Get of Fenris, Uktena, Wendigo and Bunyip.<br /> <br /> Since we've already established that Garou terms, specially the most relevant terms, were appropriated by humans, it seems logical to assume that this appropriation ocurred to the names of these Tribes. In fact, it would be absurd to think that the term Gaia came from humans, right?<br /> <br /> So, if words in general go from Garou to human and there's nothing that leads us to believe that the Tribe names are the exception to this rule, we can safely assume that the names Black Furies, Children of Gaia, Get of Fenris, Uktena, Wendigo and Bunyip were created by the Garou and learned by the humans.<br /> <br /> Unless you can you provide a canonical example that says the opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img19/986/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":2766,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","user":"Wolfen","date":". 10-11-2021, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","name":"Wolfen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T04:21:19-07:00","id":1463413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463408#post1463408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...you don't come across as talking <b>only</b> about some Tribes' names.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, my fault.I usually forget that canonically a lot of words are from Garou origin because I find the particular list of words particularly stupid, but it is, indeed, canon and I should have recognized it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463408#post1463408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it seems logical to assume that this appropriation ocurred to the names of these Tribes. In fact, it would be absurd to think that the term Gaia came from humans, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it seems logical. Yet humans could obtain these names from other sources, since those spirits don't deal only with the Garou and those tribes, as you said, are named after other entities and not just a High Tongue word, so either a confirmed link to the Garou is need or a pattern that can be observed with other tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463408#post1463408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nothing that leads us to believe that the Tribe names are the exception to this rule</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the fact that all other tribes are exceptions to this rule. Also you're forgetting Croatan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463408#post1463408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you can you provide a canonical example that says the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proof of absence? Always a hard one to provide, but I think I can try.<br /> <br /> We have no single reference of a legend or whatever coming from the names Silver Fangs, Stargazers, Shadow Lords, Silent Striders, Bone Gnawers, Red Talons, White Howlers, Black Spiral Dancers, Wardens of Apes or any of the six names the Glass Walkers had through human history.<br /> <br /> So, considering that Mages, Sorcerers and lesser shamans are also capable of learning about these spirits and have a habit of informing human cultures directly instead of culling them, and in the lack of further evidence except a list of random words that make no sense, it seems to me that the game doesn't make a case of leaking tribe names to human cultures.<br /> <br /> You can present counter proof or just keep saying that it would be logical to do something the authors didn't do? Because I agree it would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T11:56:40-07:00","id":1463447,"title":"","content":"Spirit language is universal in the canon? It is something I'm not keen to, because I am not so familiar with the setting, I'm pretty ignorant about its minutiae. <br /> 1) Is the spirit language something that every spirit in the world (and maybe universe) understands?<br /> 2) And is the Garou language the same, or is different?<br /> 3) Is it in canon said the origin of the Garou language beside the spirits? Is it somewhat meshed with something human; is it local; or is it all spiritual?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T12:27:25-07:00","id":1463450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463447#post1463447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit language is universal in the canon? It is something I'm not keen to, because I am not so familiar with the setting, I'm pretty ignorant about its minutiae.<br /> 1) Is the spirit language something that every spirit in the world (and maybe universe) understands?<br /> 2) And is the Garou language the same, or is different?<br /> 3) Is it in canon said the origin of the Garou language beside the spirits? Is it somewhat meshed with something human; is it local; or is it all spiritual?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gift Spirit Speech's description mentions a &quot;language of the spirit world&quot; in W20. And allows, I quote, &quot;for clearly understanding any spirit&quot;.<br /> <br /> The revised edition (and before, iirc) however is much different. There the Gift states, that it allows to address any spirit, whether they want to be addressed or not. It also gives an intuitive understanding of what a spirit wishes to communicate, although certain spirits might be too alien to be understood.<br /> <br /> So, as I understand it, in revised the Garou uses any human language, garou high tongue, lupine tongue or sign language to address the spirit, the gift conveys the meaning. The spirit might answer though motion, sounds, posture or breaking wind in a specific manner (that's a Dr. Who reference) - the Garou intuitively understands what the spirit means (or not, if too alien).<br /> <br /> I like revised. I hate W20's implications.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> 1. W20 implicates there might be a common language. Revised edition didn't have that. If a spirit could communicate with another spirit was totally up to the storyteller.<br /> 2. Different. In W20 it must be, because the gift wouldn't make sense otherwise. In revised, there is no shared spirit language, so it isn't the same as Garou high tongue.<br /> 3. Garou high tongue is claimed to be a Fianna invention, so it is not tied to humans or spirits, or both - just like Fianna (or the proto-tribe that later became known as Fianna).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 10-11-2021, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T14:11:34-07:00","id":1463464,"title":"","content":"#3: The High Tongue isn't a Fianna invention. All Garou have an instinctive knowledge of it upon their First Change. Since it's an innate part of them, it has to be tied to their creation, which in WtA cosmology would mean the great spirits of Gaia and Luna or the pre-imbalance Triat level of spirit. It's not something the spirits actively teach them, but something their creators put in them.<br /> <br /> That said, while there's no mechanics to this beyond rolling dice for certain skill checks that would be true for any language, the Fianna are the Tribe describe being most active in elaborating the High Tongue into a more expressive language over the base level of mutual understanding all Garou have, and spreading their version of it to the Garou Nation at large. This gets to the idea of the High Tongue developing dialects; the core language remains the same for every Garou, but artistic flair, cadence, idioms, and so on can develop among Garou communities. Russian High Tongue would be noticeably different from the Fianna based High Tongue of Europe its colonial descendant countries, as would the High Tongue of the Pure Lands, the Emerald Courts, and so on.<br /> <br /> The intrinsic core language makes sense as something that keeps them from diverging to the point of being separate languages, but otherwise this sort of drift is actually fairly normal; not just in humans, we see this in most socially verbal animals where vocalizations are taught on some level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T14:28:06-07:00","id":1463466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463464#post1463464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#3: The High Tongue isn't a Fianna invention. All Garou have an instinctive knowledge of it upon their First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are referencing the ability to communicate with wolves. Garou Tongue is taught and not before the Rite of Passage.<br /> Although, I guess, cubs and kinfolk alike will pick up some words and expressions, if they hear them often enough.<br /> <br /> See W20 page 58. I'm pretty sure it was like that in 2nd and revised, too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T16:00:35-07:00","id":1463482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463413#post1463413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, my fault.I usually forget that canonically a lot of words are from Garou origin because I find the particular list of words particularly stupid, but it is, indeed, canon and I should have recognized it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. It just reminds us that it's important to keep personal opinions in check when analyzing anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463413#post1463413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet humans could obtain these names from other sources, since those spirits don't deal only with the Garou and those tribes, as you said, are named after other entities and not just a High Tongue word, so either a confirmed link to the Garou is need or a pattern that can be observed with other tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a pretty obvious link between the Get of Fenris, Uktena, Wendigo and Bunyip and their namesake entities: the entities are the tribal totens. The Children of Gaia are named after Gaia herself and the Black Furies are named after the Erinyes, that are daughters of Gaia. It makes no sense to believe that these Tribes took their names from the human mythology instead of from the entities themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463413#post1463413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the fact that all other tribes are exceptions to this rule. Also you're forgetting Croatan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other Tribes don't have a name with any word that is of a special significance to the Garou. Since you just want to talk about &quot;the idea of some monster legends be the result of a Garou <b>tribe's name</b> trickling down to human culture&quot; there's no reason to talk about, say, the Bone Gnawers.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I didn't forget the Croatan. I left them out of my list because they are named after a mystery, almost an urban legend of sorts, but not a supernatural entity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463413#post1463413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Proof of absence? Always a hard one to provide, but I think I can try.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I didn't make myself clear. I was asking for some canonical example that says &quot;such and such words, that have specific significance for the Garou and are present on a human language, were taught by the humans to the Garou&quot;, because what the general canon says is exactly the opposite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463413#post1463413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in the lack of further evidence except a list of random words that make no sense, it seems to me that the game doesn't make a case of leaking tribe names to human cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game DOES make a case of leaking Tribe names to human cultures, exactly because it states that said &quot;words that make no sense&quot; (your opinion, not mine, and personal opinons are irrelevant) leak from Garou to human and not the other way around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463413#post1463413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can present counter proof or just keep saying that it would be logical to do something the authors didn't do?</div> </div> </div> </div>To present a counterproof I would first need a proof to counter. Again, the default situation is that in the case of relevant words the Garou influenced the humans and you gave me no evidence of the contrary.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd like to say two more things:<br /> <br /> First, I totally agree with you when you say that Forsaken handled the names in a much better way. Those names really seem ancient, I wish there was a way to bring them to the Apocalypse setting.<br /> <br /> Second, while I believe you are downplaying the cultural impact the Garou had on humans, you also seem to propose that spirits could have contacted humans and influenced their culture directly. Now, THIS is an idea I find interesting. Not the humans influencing the Garou, but spirits influencing them both independently. I think it's reasonable to believe that Fenrir, Uktena, Wendigo, Bunyip and the Erinyes may have contacted some humans directly and that we may have a lot of storytelling opportunities if we consider the cultural contrast between Garou and human mythologies and the different ways each spirit may have presented itself to these two very different societies.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img19/986/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","name":"Wolfen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T16:36:22-07:00","id":1463491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463482#post1463482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, while I believe you are downplaying the cultural impact the Garou had on humans, you also seem to propose that spirits could have contacted humans and influenced their culture directly. Now, THIS is an idea I find interesting. Not the humans influencing the Garou, but spirits influencing them both independently. I think it's reasonable to believe that Fenrir, Uktena, Wendigo, Bunyip and the Erinyes may have contacted some humans directly and that we may have a lot of storytelling opportunities if we consider the cultural contrast between Garou and human mythologies and the different ways each spirit may have presented itself to these two very different societies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly possible but I suppose it depends on how much you think the Garou are an island among humanity. Certainly, they are divorced from mankind by Rage but there are Garou who hold 9-5 jobs, Garou who go to Church, Garou who live in houses, and Garou who have families. They interact with humanity on a far more regular basis than vampires who are divorced from humanity for half of the day and are biologically distinct in a power that don't. Garou very often can vote and have social security numbers. Garou might in fact sit down and explain his religion around a campfire to humans he likes.<br /> <br /> A human will forget a Crinos form werewolf but won't forget talking with a Garou or seeing them in any other form.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T16:50:58-07:00","id":1463496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463482#post1463482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you also seem to propose that spirits could have contacted humans and influenced their culture directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my sole proposition from the beginning, I don't remember to have said that the tribes' names came from humans, but that they came from the same source (from the spirit to both the Garou and humans).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T00:31:28-07:00","id":1463547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463482#post1463482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...] and Bunyip and their namesake entities: the entities are the tribal totens.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bunyip Totem is the Rainbow Serpent, iirc.<br /> Bunyip are &quot;just&quot; an australian legend, with an origin that seems to be debated still, according to wikipedia. Although people seem to be certain, from which aboriginal group's language the word originated....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T18:41:04-07:00","id":1464441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463491#post1463491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou might in fact sit down and explain his religion around a campfire to humans he likes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agreed! Also, many kinfolk could do the same, so Rage isn't really a problem if the Garou want humans to learn parts of Garou culture and I can easily see it happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img19/986/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","name":"Wolfen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T18:51:13-07:00","id":1464443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463496#post1463496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember to have said that the tribes' names came from humans, but that they came from the same source (from the spirit to both the Garou and humans).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, these two quotes...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463496#post1463496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as far a canon goes, virtually no word trickled down from Garou culture to human culture, but the opposite happened a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463496#post1463496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the idea of some monster legends be the result of a Garou tribe's name trickling down to human culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>...seemed to indicate that you were considering a Garou tribe's name as an example of a word that could have trickled down from human culture to Garou culture. Anyway, just a misunderstanding!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img19/986/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","name":"Wolfen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T18:52:35-07:00","id":1464444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1463547#post1463547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bunyip Totem is the Rainbow Serpent, iirc.<br /> Bunyip are &quot;just&quot; an australian legend, with an origin that seems to be debated still, according to wikipedia. Although people seem to be certain, from which aboriginal group's language the word originated....</div> </div> </div> </div>At first I thought the same, but W20 (pg. 389) lists Buniyp as being the Tribal Totem...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img19/986/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","name":"Wolfen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T18:53:48-07:00","id":1464445,"title":"","content":"Crimson Thaw is finally available on DriveThru RPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/372502/World-of-Darkness-Crimson-Thaw-1?affiliate_id=10748\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/17059/372502.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/372502/World-of-Darkness-Crimson-Thaw-1?affiliate_id=10748\" target=\"_blank\"> World of Darkne