category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1470001#post1470001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think they're talking about the first two pages with the manacled prisoner. Silver damage from the manacles and anger at being contained gives you a whole bunch of Rage back without even trying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, true.<br /> <br /> I concede.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T14:41:22-08:00","id":1470164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1470001#post1470001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they're talking about the first two pages with the manacled prisoner. Silver damage from the manacles and anger at being contained gives you a whole bunch of Rage back without even trying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about W5, but I would disagree on any edition prior to that.<br /> <br /> As it is so often the case with werewolf players, frenzy triggers and instances to regain rage are mixed up:<br /> Being contained is a frenzy trigger, not an event to regain Rage.<br /> Close to silver, the same. Although RAW it is &quot;large quantities&quot; which might be the case, no idea about the comic.<br /> See page 262 of W20 for both mentions in the &quot;Frenzy&quot; section.<br /> <br /> Regaining Rage, as page 145, is limited to seeing the Moon (first time at night, which is its own problem if the moon is visible only at daytime and dusk/dawn), being humiliated (which might bring back one dot, if being taken prisoner by the vamp is that humiliating, which might or might not be the case, imo, depending on the circumstances), botches and anticipation of a confrontation (that is, a fight, usually one initiated by the garou). I'd wager, anticipation of being executed doesn't really allow to regain rage. In any case, humiliation and anticipation of confrontation are RAW limited to one dot. So, no bunch of Rage, whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Supernatural powers not withstanding, regeneration of more than one Rage only happens when a new story starts out of a downtime period, or it the garou sees the moon, as mentioned above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T20:35:16-08:00","id":1470185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1470164#post1470164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure about W5, but I would disagree on any edition prior to that.<br /> <br /> As it is so often the case with werewolf players, frenzy triggers and instances to regain rage are mixed up:<br /> Being contained is a frenzy trigger, not an event to regain Rage.<br /> Close to silver, the same. Although RAW it is &quot;large quantities&quot; which might be the case, no idea about the comic.<br /> See page 262 of W20 for both mentions in the &quot;Frenzy&quot; section.<br /> <br /> Regaining Rage, as page 145, is limited to seeing the Moon (first time at night, which is its own problem if the moon is visible only at daytime and dusk/dawn), being humiliated (which might bring back one dot, if being taken prisoner by the vamp is that humiliating, which might or might not be the case, imo, depending on the circumstances), botches and anticipation of a confrontation (that is, a fight, usually one initiated by the garou). I'd wager, anticipation of being executed doesn't really allow to regain rage. In any case, humiliation and anticipation of confrontation are RAW limited to one dot. So, no bunch of Rage, whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Supernatural powers not withstanding, regeneration of more than one Rage only happens when a new story starts out of a downtime period, or it the garou sees the moon, as mentioned above.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh, theres a whole bunch of things mentioned in the ST text that give opportunities to regain Rage that don't appear on the Rage chart, even more in W20 as it cut the chart even shorter.<br /> <br /> Either way, even with the extremely miserly rules of W20 your gaining a minimum of 2 Rage from humiliation and anticipation of a fight, pretty sure shifting to Crinos, losing your hands in the process and leaping out of a chair to attack a vampire counts as a confrontation in anyones book. Which is enough to allow shifting and at least one extra action....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key"