/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1471830#post1471830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All right. Is it mentioned somewhere in the books? Just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apocalypse page 32 notes Caine as EoS, specifically as a suggestion rather than hard equivalence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T00:52:16-08:00","id":1471911,"title":"","content":"Thank You! So I guess my idea about Croatan isn't possible. So Ghost Council could be Uktena or something new,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T19:09:18-08:00","id":1473622,"title":"","content":"The theory is ghost council is uktena. My person thought is maybe it\u2019s the remnants of the not fallen wendigo and the uktena merged. I only assume the wendigo due to their name being blacked out in the comic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T19:11:05-08:00","id":1473623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1470411#post1470411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, taking a look at the Celerity for V5, if Rage is kept as a peer of it, Garou could have the pants-shitting capacity to just blink through the air and appear in front of their foes. This, in addition to bullet time dodging, better chasing capacity, or comparable powers etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly what I\u2019m thinking will happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T07:30:26-08:00","id":1473653,"title":"","content":"Rage I see as working more as a Blood Surge than a discipline power, or letting you use full dice pools against multiple foes (or get a bonus for a single one, or get a bonus you use as you want, either singly or dividing through opponents). But I got no clue honestly, may there will be really different uses, either for damage, dice or speed (which in a combat without much importance to initiative order is mostly a penalty cutter for minor actions).<br /> <br /> But I'm interested to see how they do this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T13:03:35-07:00","id":1478409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461116#post1461116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coyotes are as similar to wolves as jackals, while the Thylacine isn't even next to the <i>Canidae</i>. Yet jackals and thylacines are Garou tribes, but coyotes aren't.<br /> <br /> Sure...</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. If jackals get a tribe in the form of the Silent Striders and we can have Bone Gnawers &amp; Glass Walkers playing hopscotch in the blurry lines between wolf and dog, it's only fair for the Nuwisha to be a Garou tribe. Never actually got to ST anything set in Australia, but dealt with this in some (very, very) old notes of mine by making <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dingo\" target=\"_blank\">dingoes</a> and related species in nearby islands into an aboriginal garou tribe, with the thylacines as a Fera breed of their own that was strongly connected to the Bunyip tribe until their destruction by human and foreign Garou competition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1461116#post1461116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way it's in the text I thinking it is less that a tribe left and more that it is quieter among the Garou, which is different from what the Stargazers did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, sometimes i'm divided on the matter and half tempted to keep the Nuwisha as they are and make them and the &quot;dingo Bunyip&quot; into a set of &quot;apocryphal tribes/breeds&quot;, along with some homebrew groups based on dholes, african wild dogs and maybe some other canines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-09-2022, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T17:26:06-07:00","id":1478448,"title":"","content":"Nuwisha are a separate breed because development decisions wanted them to not have Rage and hence think in a way that was dramatically different from the wolves. Are you a warrior that's kind of a trickster? Ragabash. A trickster that wears a lot of hats to get things done? Nuwisha.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the two ended up fused as a retcon in 5e, and the lack of the Garou mating with Garou prohibition is a result of it, as the Nuwisha didn't play like that. This could also play into Rage working very differently. That, however, is kind of a radical departure from the past, so I wouldn't find it too terribly likely, even given the first tenet of the litany getting axed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T04:50:31-07:00","id":1479538,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't understand why Uktena couldn't be kept as a tribe name (if Ghost Council turns to be Uktena)<br /> but I'm ignorant about the nuances of native american cultures so it might be something that is offensive?<br /> Wasn't it the name of some ancient spirit or god of native american tribes of old?<br /> <br /> I'm supposing that's the case, but I'm not much fond of bland renaming (looking at you, &quot;the Ministry&quot;)<br /> Also wouldn't be better &quot;Ghost Councilors&quot; or &quot;Ghost Advisors&quot; or &quot;Ghost Mentors&quot; or &quot;Ghost Monitors&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T07:19:38-07:00","id":1479543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479538#post1479538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't understand why Uktena couldn't be kept as a tribe name</div> </div> </div> </div>Native Americans IRL specifically asked to drop it. Not by far as intensely as they asked to drop <i>Wendigo</i>, but still. Yes, it is offensive.<br /> <br /> Main reasons:<br /> <br /> 1 - Only those two tribes used their patron's name directly as tribal name. While apparently subtle, this is a fine example of exoticization;<br /> <br /> 2 - The authors had zero understanding of what the spirit meant in its original culture and general cultural context, just used a White Pop Culture understanding of it without ever consulting a Native opinion, which is problematic in several levels;<br /> <br /> 3 - It broadly applies to all Natives a name that actually belongs to only one tribe, without regards to any nuance on how diverse and distinct the cultures of the several Native nations are. It is as if there were only two European Tribes called Broxa and Chernobog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T19:43:41-07:00","id":1479569,"title":"","content":"I must say, the whole thing of Werewolf with indigenous people seemed many times less of a &quot;here, this is important and very interesting, let's give you some of its concepts with respect through the mold of our game about werewolfs&quot;, and more like &quot;hey, do you know indians like to throw tomahawks, wear feathers and summons spirits, pretty neat huh guys? would you like to be from the Boogeyman tribe?&quot;. And yeah, i'm making an exaggerated example, but it was the impression I got when I first read WtA 2nd edition, and just got less of that in W20. <br /> <br /> And the global communion and ecumenism of the Garou seems more absurd than the a worldwide organization of the Camarilla, that is in itself, much more individualistic and parochial than the Garou Nation, which seems like a stupid concept for me (but please, I can be a Grinch with Werewolf the Apocalypse, but in no way I think those who like and appreciate it are like the opinion I have of what they like). <br /> <br /> I'm pretty curious of how I personally will like W5 and how many longtime fans will receive it. I have a friend who loves Werewolf, and STelled us a 3-shot of W20 recently, and I'll want to see what he thinks of it. There is a lot they can make more &quot;politically&quot; correct, and the way WoD is going more agnostic in 5th edition, I wonder how the super gnostic and animistic setting of Werewolf will be, maybe it will be an exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T23:37:03-07:00","id":1479574,"title":"","content":"The 'Garou Nation' as a term for all of garou-kind has been around for a long time. But earlier in WtA's publication history the setting seemed to be more localised, with each sept being kind of unique and the game being quite different, depending on where you set the game to take place. With the tribebooks came kind of templates how tribal septs might work and it removed some of the individualism. The remark that there are local rules held in the same regard as tenets of the Litany is still there in 2nd Edition and iirc revised, but it is not given any example in the supplements, at least not that I remember.<br /> With revised and W20 came even more globalisation into the Setting. Which might make sense, as the Garou are basically a secret organisation that has a desire to communicate between septs. Even if they still would only use Silent Striders as delivery man, they could consume human news broadcasts from all over the world and aren't as oblivious to things that happen far away, as they might have been 200 years prior.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't like this global garou nation connotation. But the terms meaning has shifted over the editions, as the Setting's focus changed.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> As for the Native American tribe's names. I think it is okay to change them, as long as it is framed as something that happened over the last two decades or so, but i would not totally hate a retcon on this, too, for it is a correction of a design flaw in the Setting.<br /> <br /> That said, I find an approach to reduce the stereotypes in many cases rather unfruitful. I mean, sure, there is merit to show that the fictional werewolf tribe culture is more diverse than attributes described to highlight stereotypes one might attribute to Native Americans,.... or people of Irish descent (drunk Fianna), or eastern European descent (all un-trustworthy cut-throats), or Asian descent (philosophical Kung-Fu masters) or Italian descent (Wise Guys Glass Walkers) or what ever other stereotypes there are.<br /> <br /> But, stereotypes didn't just spring into existence. There is a reason they developed - which might have more or less truth at it's core. And for a work of fiction, one has to give the text some freedom to explore and use these stereotypes and build character archetypes around them. For, it is a tabletop role playing game and has a need to describe some easily understandable roles. Using stereotypes and archetypes is a legit way to do this. Ever read casting calls for actors? They often describe roles using such expressions. Nuance is added to character roles later, the template has to be more generic.<br /> WtA is not a thesis for a anthropology PhD and shouldn't aim to be. Sidebars elaborating on topics the descriptions might neglect, are totally fine, though.<br /> <br /> But, that said, I find that the reproach that KotE is orientalism might be objectively correct, but still it is something that I want and need of that Setting. A disclaimer or warning that the game is that way could have been helpful. And sure, the Setting might mix a lot of East-Asian culture, legend, myth, philosophy into a potpourri of a game Setting. But so do all the Core game lines to some extend.<br /> <br /> When <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> said, the two Native American tribes are as if there were only two European tribes I thought, that's true. But come to think of it, there are three Native American tribes in the Setting - and the Coratans might have been subject an unfortunate name choice, too. But there are also only a few tribes which borrow of European cultures, too. That the Get's mixture of stereotypical Viking culture with 20th century Nazi Germany is a mess we already discussed. Besides that the Fianna borrow extensively from stereotypes attributed to Irish immigrants to America. The Irish aren't necessarily attributed like the Fianna in Germany (apart from American TV Shows). The Black Furies borrow from the Greek myths and symbolism, but are hardly attributed a lot of stereotypes usually associated with the Greek. The Wise Guys too borrow from Mafia-type archetypes, but hardly other stereotypes associated with the Italian. The Shadow Lords mainly follow a generic character stereotype than actual stereotypes associated with the region the tribe is said to originate from. Same is true for Silver Fang houses and Red Talons. Children of Gaia borrow from stereotypes of a sub-culture mainly, not necessarily from a human culture of a given region or nation.<br /> <br /> So, should I be offended about the fact that Nazi Germany is the main (but not only) fallback whenever stereotypical German elements are used in a character. Germans are often described as meticulous and punctual. Try to add that to the Gets.<br /> What about the French and Spanish? Are thy represented in WtA tribes? Not really. The Spanish are all Lasombra anyway.<br /> The Portuguese and Netherlandish? Well, the later are at least probably housing a Silver Fang house, right?<br /> <br /> So, does it do the Native American tribes and Nations justice that they are only represented in two living and one dead tribe? Most likely not.<br /> Could it be done better? Probably.<br /> Is a more or less complete description of the diverse and distinct Native American cultures necessary within the need of a tabletop role-playing game to convey character concepts and archetypes? A more generic description might be sufficient, I think.<br /> Could the different Native American tribes be handled better (within the scope of a tabletop RPG) by reverting to WtA's 1st Edition's focus on local sept's differences and local distinctions? Maybe.<br /> Could the different cultures of East-Asia with the general KotE Setting be handled better by adding distinct groups of Hsien, Hengeyokai, Mages, Bygone, Chimera, whatever, but still leave the overall Setting intact? Maybe.<br /> <br /> Is using the word &quot;werewolf&quot; from the Proto-West-Germanic language cultural appropriation and should the game be henceforth called &quot;Lycantroph: the Nit-Picking&quot;? Hopefully not.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 04-27-2022, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T01:13:45-07:00","id":1479577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479574#post1479574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'Garou Nation' as a term for all of garou-kind has been around for a long time. But earlier in WtA's publication history the setting seemed to be more localised, with each sept being kind of unique and the game being quite different, depending on where you set the game to take place. With the tribebooks came kind of templates how tribal septs might work and it removed some of the individualism. The remark that there are local rules held in the same regard as tenets of the Litany is still there in 2nd Edition and iirc revised, but it is not given any example in the supplements, at least not that I remember.<br /> With revised and W20 came even more globalisation into the Setting. Which might make sense, as the Garou are basically a secret organisation that has a desire to communicate between septs. Even if they still would only use Silent Striders as delivery man, they could consume human news broadcasts from all over the world and aren't as oblivious to things that happen far away, as they might have been 200 years prior.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't like this global garou nation connotation. But the terms meaning has shifted over the editions, as the Setting's focus changed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, one of the beauties with WtA is that each sept and its members is unique from another. Nevermind garou from different countries.<br /> <br /> Heck, they would not even use the same names as most tribe names are generic descriptions. In Finland, we would not have Get of Fenris, Black Furies and Silver Fangs running about. We would have Fenriksen Suku, Mustat Raivottared and Hopeaveitset.<br /> <br /> While the tribes would follow the same totem, they would be affected by the local culture as well. My long-term house rule for garou in Finland is that a totem Bear would not gain negative renown because Bear is a sacred animal here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T02:16:59-07:00","id":1479578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479574#post1479574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I find an approach to reduce the stereotypes in many cases rather unfruitful.</div> </div> </div> </div>We could argue at length about stereotypes and how much they help or harm the setting, be them about natives or any other group, but that's not actually the question. The question is, indeed, <u>the names</u> and the connotations <u>they</u> carry. And again, this is an issue that actual members of the First Nations from several tribes, including the actual tribes from where those name were took, asked to be solved that way because of the subjects it touches for them.<br /> <br /> General problems with stereotypes also exist, but they're another issue, with its own considerations, including the ones you put.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479574#post1479574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, stereotypes didn't just spring into existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and they indeed have a place in fiction. But we do have to evaluate what their particular implications are, which groups they affect, and when it is time to drop them because they're starting to do more harm than help.<br /> <br /> Because while stereotypes can be used as narrative tools, they're also mental constructs real people apply in real life to other real people, with real consequences. Bullying, profiling, persecution, job offers, self-esteem, many aspects of someone's life can be affected by stereotypes, so fiction does have to own its responsibility in propagating or deconstructing such stereotypes based on their real life effects.<br /> <br /> Do not conflate stereotypes with archetypes either, they're not the same thing. An archetype is a simple idea of character loosely defined by a short description. A stereotype is a generalization on how a group of people looks like and/or behave. The Donut Eater Cop is an Archetype. Depicting all your cops as donut eaters is a stereotype (that may come with the full capital Donut Eater archetype or not).<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb stereotypes are bad, despite being really hard to get rid entirely, and that includes all the stereotypes you cited. But I don't think it hard to understand that Native Americans need special attention because they <b><u>ARE</u></b> currently far more vulnerable. They're more vulnerable than black Americans, and those are almost literally being actively hunted by cops and neo-nazi jerks. While it must be really awful to be of Irish descent in the US and everyone think you're a drunkard by default, I don't think they need the same urgency.now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479574#post1479574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WtA is not a thesis for a anthropology PhD and shouldn't aim to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should aim to not offend people particularly tired of racist stereotypes, though, be them from a Cherokee village or from Sicily. Not using a name you're specifically asked not to is particularly good form in general.<br /> <br /> And we live in the 21st century, asking an actual member of the group in question isn't really hard anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479574#post1479574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, that said, I find that the reproach that KotE is orientalism might be objectively correct, but still it is something that I want and need of that Setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it harms real people because of this, and they think changing it is the best way to solve the problem, what you want becomes irrelevant, because their well-being is also objectively more important than your game, and no disclaimer will change it (unless the disclaimer <b>is</b> the actual best solution, but if the solution is to drop it, drop it).<br /> <br /> The whole point is that there are actual people facing actual problems, and those people should be consulted. Solving the real problems that arise from cultural bias is more important, period, but also should be done with their participation. KotE is still an open question among Asian players, and a &quot;solution&quot; is being attempted without consulting them, which is wrong. The Metis' elimination affects disabled people and as far as anyone can tell disabled people weren't consulted on their elimination, either.<br /> <br /> But the drop on the tribal names of the &quot;Pure&quot; Tribes is a direct request of Native Americans, and one without significant contention among them, it is easy to find many texts about the issue on the internet written by natives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479574#post1479574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there are also only a few tribes which borrow of European cultures, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point isn't if they borrow from European culture, it is that the game has a lot of European tribes and they cover a lot of themes and archetypes instead of being only defined by their culture, then Africa, America and Asia have Ethnic Stereotype Tribes. So the variety of the Tribes was birthed in Europe while other parts of the world just give rise to <i>exotic folk</i>.<br /> <br /> If the game effectively had only Ethnic Redux tribes all over the place, then the problem would actually be less so. Far less, although the real problems they cause could still not be proportional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479574#post1479574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, should I be offended about the fact that Nazi Germany is the main (but not only) fallback whenever stereotypical German elements are used in a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only one who can say if you should is you, but if you did, then it would be your right and something to be taken into account.<br /> <br /> By the way, the Get didn't started as stereotypical Nazis, or even as Germans, they're archetypal Modern Vikings. The nazi thing got added later and it is precisely its stereotyping that ended with Paradox deciding to make them a Fallen tribe. So the original was not so much of a stereotype, but you can bet new Get will be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479574#post1479574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, does it do the Native American tribes and Nations justice that they are only represented in two living and one dead tribe? Most likely not.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one questioned their number. They questioned their names.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479574#post1479574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A more generic description might be sufficient, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Like Ghost Council.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479574#post1479574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the different Native American tribes be handled better (within the scope of a tabletop RPG) by reverting to WtA's 1st Edition's focus on local sept's differences and local distinctions? Maybe.<br /> Could the different cultures of East-Asia with the general KotE Setting be handled better by adding distinct groups of Hsien, Hengeyokai, Mages, Bygone, Chimera, whatever, but still leave the overall Setting intact? Maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about consulting actual Native Americans for the first and actual Asians (preferably from several countries) for the later before and during the process of handling them? That's all you actually need to do, not to try to find a solution to a world crisis on your own.<br /> <br /> This is the White Knight Complex, and its argumentative cousin Too Complex To Solve. The problem seems incredibly complex so that it is impractical or impossible to be solved, but it is actually quite simple, the problem is the very fact that the White Savior is trying to solve other people's problems instead of just invite them to the discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T02:18:34-07:00","id":1479579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479574#post1479574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't like this global garou nation connotation. But the terms meaning has shifted over the editions, as the Setting's focus changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also just the growing acknowledgement that the older focus of the setting is even more non-sense than usual for the WoD.<br /> <br /> Even in 1e, Moon Bridges allowed the Garou to have a trade and communication network for thousands of years before humans would get anywhere close. A level 5 Caern can generate Moon Bridges with a range of 10,000 miles (which is just shy of anywhere on Earth: the records for farthest apart cities are ~12,500 miles), and Garou treat it as 1/1000 the distance, so the longest moon bridges are the same as a 10 mile hike (considerable for an average modern urban living human, but nothing for a wolf or a particularly fit homid). When packs can travel across Europe in under 10 minutes, the idea of each Sept being highly idiosyncratic gets hard to suspend disbelief over. There was plenty of diversity within the Roman Empire, but the Romans still made sure each major city shared certain cultural norms and standards, making the empire cohesive across its vast reach... and they didn't have Moon Bridges, just normal roads and animal drawn wagons.<br /> <br /> The only way for the Three Brothers to actually stay apart from the rest of the Garou for so long is for them to have actively resisted attempts to establish Moon Bridges to Asia or Europe. The Garou have other ways to get somewhere, the Eurasian Garou had the departure of the Three Brothers as part of their oral histories, and IRL there is ample archeological evidence of regular trade from South America to at least the Philippines and Indonesia via Pacific islands, and keeping the Red Talons from crossing the Arctic to find new wolves to breed with for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I find an approach to reduce the stereotypes in many cases rather unfruitful. I mean, sure, there is merit to show that the fictional werewolf tribe culture is more diverse than attributes described to highlight stereotypes one might attribute to Native Americans,.... or people of Irish descent (drunk Fianna), or eastern European descent (all un-trustworthy cut-throats), or Asian descent (philosophical Kung-Fu masters) or Italian descent (Wise Guys Glass Walkers) or what ever other stereotypes there are. </div> </div> </div>Sorry if I can't find it at the moment, but ArcaneArts did an excellent post on the differences between stereotypes and archetypes regarding how to construct stories. It's important that WtA preserve the archetypes that make it special. The stereotypes are far less important in how to define the setting (as color to flush out the setting and how different groups feel about each other is a different thing).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> said, the two Native American tribes are as if there were only two European tribes I thought, that's true. But come to think of it, there are three Native American tribes in the Setting - and the Coratans might have been subject an unfortunate name choice, too. </div> </div> </div>Counting the Croatoan just lets you count the White Howlers as another purely European Tribe if you want to discuss ones that don't exist in the present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But there are also only a few tribes which borrow of European cultures, too. </div> </div> </div>I think there's a big disconnect here between the in-universe nature of the Tribes, and how they were constructed. From a Watsonian view, yes, there aren't many distinctly European Tribes, and most of the Tribes are stated to have either started elsewhere or spread far beyond Europe in their histories. From a Doylist perspective, lots of the more &quot;global&quot; Tribes are still crafted from a heavily European/Western lens. The Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, and Glass Walkers might have much more extensive in-universe roots, but the reality of how they're written in the books is very European. Even the Stargazers and Silent Striders have much more to do with European rooted stereotyping than they do with trying to portray what Garou from those circumstances would really be like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Try to add that to the Gets. </div> </div> </div>The Germanic-including Silver Fang House Gleaming Eye largely stole that bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about the French and Spanish? Are thy represented in WtA tribes? </div> </div> </div>Originally Fianna, as the Fianna covered most of Western Europe until the Punic Wars and steadily lost ground to the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords over the centuries (presumably with some Get help as the Germanic Franks displaced the Fianna's Gaulish kin in France). Houses Wyrmfoe and Unbreakable Hearth were the dominate Silver Fangs in France after Conquering Claw died out, until they opted to take the Americas instead, leaving most of France, Belgium, Netherlands, and Luxembourg in Gleaming Eye's hands, while the Shadow Lords dominated the Garou holdings in the Iberian peninsula (not super well explained how that happened, but presumably they used the Reconquista).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is using the word &quot;werewolf&quot; from the Proto-West-Germanic language cultural appropriation... </div> </div> </div>No.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T04:41:04-07:00","id":1479580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479578#post1479578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We could argue at length about stereotypes and how much they help or harm the setting, be them about natives or any other group, but that's not actually the question. The question is, indeed, <u>the names</u> and the connotations <u>they</u> carry. And again, this is an issue that actual members of the First Nations from several tribes, including the actual tribes from where those name were took, asked to be solved that way because of the subjects it touches for them.<br /> <br /> General problems with stereotypes also exist, but they're another issue, with its own considerations, including the ones you put.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> &quot;Ghost Council&quot; is fine with me, if it keeps other aspects of the tribe intact. If they change the tribe to retroactively to match some qualities that one might derive from the new name, I wounldn't like it.<br /> I mean, why &quot;Ghost&quot;, not spirit? And why &quot;Council&quot;? Despite the fact that it might be name of a camp that is less problematic IRL then the Uktena name, the new name doesn't do anything for me, except giving me a headache when imagining how it will be translated to the German version of the game. For Spirit and Ghost could both be translated to &quot;Geist&quot;, but a ghost could also be translated to &quot;Gespenst&quot; which is more what one could call a &quot;Poltergeist&quot; and what within the WoD is a wraith - which in turn is nothing the 'Ghost Council' should be too concerned with, for that is Silent Strider domain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479578#post1479578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a rule of thumb stereotypes are bad, despite being really hard to get rid entirely, and that includes all the stereotypes you cited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that so? In German archetype is rarely used, as a word, although it is derived from Greek origin and nominally part of the German language. Stereotype is used more often, but not necessarily meaning that they are bad. Preconception, on the other hand, is the word describing such mental constructs, that usually carries a bad connotation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479578#post1479578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we live in the 21st century, asking an actual member of the group in question isn't really hard anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. As with any group, asking a member is hardly a representative study and I'd imagine a lot of people from Native American communities have a lot of more pressing problems than the misuse of a word from their culture in a RPG and related media, but like I said I have no problem with the name change in general, not even as a retcon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the KotE situation, I wish they would find collaborators from Asia and salvage the Setting instead of spreading western Vampires or Garou to the east and make VtM and WtA globally correct descriptions of the social structure and supernatural mechanics.<br /> Same goes for Ebony Kindom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479579#post1479579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also just the growing acknowledgement that the older focus of the setting is even more non-sense than usual for the WoD.<br /> <br /> Even in 1e, Moon Bridges allowed the Garou to have a trade and communication network for thousands of years before humans would get anywhere close. A level 5 Caern can generate Moon Bridges with a range of 10,000 miles (which is just shy of anywhere on Earth: the records for farthest apart cities are ~12,500 miles), and Garou treat it as 1/1000 the distance, so the longest moon bridges are the same as a 10 mile hike (considerable for an average modern urban living human, but nothing for a wolf or a particularly fit homid). When packs can travel across Europe in under 10 minutes, the idea of each Sept being highly idiosyncratic gets hard to suspend disbelief over. There was plenty of diversity within the Roman Empire, but the Romans still made sure each major city shared certain cultural norms and standards, making the empire cohesive across its vast reach... and they didn't have Moon Bridges, just normal roads and animal drawn wagons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Ages Werewolf lists 5.000 miles and the distance might have been even shorter earlier in time. We also don't know how the availability of Path Stones developed over time (but I remember reading there were wars between septs fought over those).<br /> It is less than 100km from my home town to France. Sure, there is and always was cultural exchange but also two World Wars until in 1992 the EU was formed out of a trade/toll-union. So, the tribe's couldn't even decide on a code of conduct until the representatives made the journey to Pangea, shed their tribal affiliations and came up the tenets condensed of the Litany of stories they all considered important. It is not that much suspension of disbelieve needed to imagine, that local septs could still be pretty different all over the world, even if belonging to the same tribe.<br /> <br /> I mean, since my childhood I'm influenced a lot by US TV shows, but I like to think I'm still quite different from the average American. Or someone from northern Germany, even.<br /> I mean, even for the Garou back in the day, the trade might have happened by Silent Strider - the UPS of times past.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479579#post1479579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if I can't find it at the moment, but ArcaneArts did an excellent post on the differences between stereotypes and archetypes regarding how to construct stories. It's important that WtA preserve the archetypes that make it special. The stereotypes are far less important in how to define the setting (as color to flush out the setting and how different groups feel about each other is a different thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you find it, I will make an effort to read it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479579#post1479579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a big disconnect here between the in-universe nature of the Tribes, and how they were constructed. From a Watsonian view, yes, there aren't many distinctly European Tribes, and most of the Tribes are stated to have either started elsewhere or spread far beyond Europe in their histories. From a Doylist perspective, lots of the more &quot;global&quot; Tribes are still crafted from a heavily European/Western lens. The Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, and Glass Walkers might have much more extensive in-universe roots, but the reality of how they're written in the books is very European. Even the Stargazers and Silent Striders have much more to do with European rooted stereotyping than they do with trying to portray what Garou from those circumstances would really be like.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But what would one expect from an American writer team producing a game for the American market.<br /> <br /> One can only imagine, if the game would have never talked about Europe, Africa, Asia or the near East and local teams would have come up with their own versions of the games here, and reconciled them all before publishing them...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479579#post1479579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Germanic-including Silver Fang House Gleaming Eye largely stole that bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, right, the meticulous and punctual inquisitor-like avengers, who might or might not have ridded themselves from the corruption amongst their own ranks. I can get onboard with those <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479579#post1479579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Originally Fianna, as the Fianna covered most of Western Europe until the Punic Wars and steadily lost ground to the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords over the centuries (presumably with some Get help as the Germanic Franks displaced the Fianna's Gaulish kin in France). Houses Wyrmfoe and Unbreakable Hearth were the dominate Silver Fangs in France after Conquering Claw died out, until they opted to take the Americas instead, leaving most of France, Belgium, Netherlands, and Luxembourg in Gleaming Eye's hands, while the Shadow Lords dominated the Garou holdings in the Iberian peninsula (not super well explained how that happened, but presumably they used the Reconquista).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the detailed in-universe description. What I meant was why there are no tribes specifically tied to stereotypes or cliches about those countries - from a development standpoint. Was a baguette-wielding mime not a suitable template for a werewolf tribe? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T06:12:16-07:00","id":1479583,"title":"","content":"Honestly, while to me WtA has a much more interesting concept than WtF, the fact that the Tribes are heavily tied to specific cultures, along with the most likely accidental implication that Europe has more cultural diversity than any other continent. It's not an inherently unsolvable issue, but still a bit annoying.<br /> <br /> Like we can apparently lump all of Asia into one tribe but need two Celtic ones (even if one of them is dead). WtA is kind of just filled with problematic implications stemming from the tying of tribes to both real world groups and archetypes. Yes camps solve some of the diversity issues, but they do nothing for others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 04-27-2022, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T12:04:04-07:00","id":1479596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479583#post1479583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, while to me WtA has a much more interesting concept than WtF, the fact that the Tribes are heavily tied to specific cultures, along with the most likely accidental implication that Europe has more cultural diversity than any other continent. It's not an inherently unsolvable issue, but still a bit annoying.<br /> <br /> Like we can apparently lump all of Asia into one tribe but need two Celtic ones (even if one of them is dead). WtA is kind of just filled with problematic implications stemming from the tying of tribes to both real world groups and archetypes. Yes camps solve some of the diversity issues, but they do nothing for others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asia used to be represented by a lot more, but the writing in Revised for some reason decided to focus entirely on the Hakken and Stargazers, playing up a rivalry with extremely cheap heat. Prior work painted a different picture - in addition to the Silver Fang house of the Blood Red Crest, Caerns: Places of Power also set down, at the bare minimum, the presence of Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers, as they are supposed to follow humanity around as a whole and not actually of a specific ethnic group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T14:35:45-07:00","id":1479602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479580#post1479580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, why &quot;Ghost&quot;, not spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's a direct reference to The Ghost Dance, a wide-spread inter-tribal spiritual movement by Native Americans to protest European expansionism and genocide and promote peaceful interactions between cultures. Ghost is most commonly used in translation because the word in the language where the movement started essentially means &quot;ancestor spirit&quot; as in the spirits of departed humans that the dance is meant to seek aid from, instead of other sorts of spirits. Using spirit would lose the connotations of fighting for cultural heritage and survival in the face of oppression.<br /> <br /> Leaving it untranslated would be hard given how few people are familiar with indigenous North American languages to have a clue of what to associate that with.<br /> <br /> Of course Ghost Dance has other pitfalls that might not be well suited to reference if not done carefully (aka with input from people that know these things at an expert level).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dark Ages Werewolf lists 5.000 miles and the distance might have been even shorter earlier in time. </div> </div> </div>I don't think you're really appreciating what these sorts of distances mean when were discussing the ability of the Garou to have a relatively consistent normalized culture between Septs.<br /> <br /> You also don't seem to be appreciating the time frames we're talking about. You're talking about cultural exchange between cultures that are basically only a few centuries old (France in 2022 is not anything like France in 12222), while many of the Garou Tribes have changed exceedingly little over thousands of years. If you went back in time 500 years, to the place you live now, people wouldn't be speaking the same language (though yes, similar) and would be a vastly different culture from what you're used to. Modern France would definitely seem a lot more relatable to you than that. A Silver Fang can go back in time 5,000 years, communicate easily, and find that the &quot;alpha&quot; Tribe really hasn't changed much in general attitudes and philosophies.<br /> <br /> Yes I focused on moon bridges, because that's about different Septs and how easily they can access each other for exchange and trade. The Garou have lots of other tools that make cultural drift less impactful than it is in humans... like the ability to just ask your great-great-grandparents how they handled things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you find it, I will make an effort to read it. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301240#post1301240\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301240#post1301240\"> On the Problematic Nature of Beast (And Why I Think That's a Good Thing) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301240#post1301240\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301240#post1301240 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> [So, after some sober reflection, I realized that I said some things in this post that I would prefer a public audience not know about me. Alors consider this an </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True. But what would one expect from an American writer team producing a game for the American market. </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about if the mistakes made 30 years ago were understandable. I'm talking about what to do with the game now that it's 30 years later and we understand those mistakes for what they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks for the detailed in-universe description. What I meant was why there are no tribes specifically tied to stereotypes or cliches about those countries - from a development standpoint. Was a baguette-wielding mime not a suitable template for a werewolf tribe? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Again, House Gleaming Eye.<br /> <br /> But also? The US doesn't actually have particularly strong stereotypes around most European cultures. Why isn't there a Tribe with Portuguese stereotypes? Because aforementioned US writers didn't actually have any stereotypes about Portuguese people to base a Tribe on. There isn't some idea of Portuguese culture in the US cultural mindset. There's a reason why US stereotypes around eastern Europe are about a giant area of the continent and not individual countries and cultures: people here don't know enough to even start to form more specific stereotypes.<br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479583#post1479583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, while to me WtA has a much more interesting concept than WtF, the fact that the Tribes are heavily tied to specific cultures, along with the most likely accidental implication that Europe has more cultural diversity than any other continent. It's not an inherently unsolvable issue, but still a bit annoying.<br /> <br /> Like we can apparently lump all of Asia into one tribe but need two Celtic ones (even if one of them is dead). WtA is kind of just filled with problematic implications stemming from the tying of tribes to both real world groups and archetypes. Yes camps solve some of the diversity issues, but they do nothing for others.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've waxed on about a lot in previous threads: the problem is that WtA has two ideas of what a Tribe is. The games have, so far, never settled on one idea of what makes a Tribe, or fully explore the implications of two distinct ideas of Tribe existing and how that impacts Garou culture.<br /> <br /> Camps are a useful solution to resolving the definition of Tribe to one concept, because Camps can then take up the roles dropped. If you make Tribes more like the Silver Fangs and Bone Gnawers - groups attached to archetypes rather than specific cultures - Camps (or Houses for Silver Fangs) step in to take on the culturally or geographically linked parts of Garou society.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T15:43:00-07:00","id":1479605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479580#post1479580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, why &quot;Ghost&quot;, not spirit? And why &quot;Council&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> covered well the Ghost Dance. About &quot;<b>Council</b>&quot;, this is the default translation for the terms the First Nations actually use in North America to define their inter-tribal organizations. They had this kind of institution to help ease relations between tribes or reduce violence in times of war way before the American settlers arrived, and currently still keep Tribal Councils as inter-tribal organs to help ease relations and pool resources where they need it.<br /> <br /> So while we don't know what will be made of them in the game yet, at first Ghost Council makes a lot of actual sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479580#post1479580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that so? In German archetype is rarely used, as a word</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be that in German the two words got conflated, that kind of thing happens sometimes. But in English (and Portuguese, I can attest), they're really distinct, and while subtle the distinction is <b><i>extremely</i></b> important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479580#post1479580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with any group, asking a member is hardly a representative study and I'd imagine a lot of people from Native American communities have a lot of more pressing problems than the misuse of a word from their culture in a RPG and related media,</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't ask a random. There are things like representatives and consultants. If you want to go cheap you seek a representative, a person that takes on themselves the responsibility to understand their own group as much as possible to bridge this kind of gap, either as voluntary work or hired by some governance body within the group. If you want to be certain you hire a consultant, a person whose work is precisely to help you understand what you need to understand for your purposes.<br /> <br /> Those are professionals being paid to do the heavy-lift of proper a study, not random people being interviewed in the streets. And they're not that hard to find and hire, even with the caveat of wanting specifically consultants on a given ethnic group no one sought out before. Which is not the case with the First Nations, instead they keep <b>several</b> certified bodies of consultants and even free services for consultation on cultural implications.<br /> <br /> All minorities and countries I know of have those kinds of services because being understood is kind of our goal. The only way to not know that such services exist is to never have asked, which is perfectly fine for you, who're just discussing things in a forum, but is inexcusable for a media company talking going global with their IP and putting money on it. Consultation is a minor cost that should just be a part of the process.<br /> <br /> If you're interested in, countries generally have such services at their embassies or equivalent outpost, they help authors, scholars and potential travelers to their country, most actually help anyone who asks, at least in some way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479580#post1479580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the KotE situation, I wish they would find collaborators from Asia and salvage the Setting</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of Asian players would like the same as you, actually, I don't know if they're a majority or not (but i have a guess). But here Paradox already made their mind as it seems and you won't be happy with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479580#post1479580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Ages Werewolf lists 5.000 miles and the distance might have been even shorter earlier in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, the point isn't in the specific numbers. Werewolf established too soon that the Garou have a hugely stable culture, with little change through time, they share most myths and the core of their religion, they have a global spanning war in their hands, and they have access to several tools to ease interactions between them. Those are global premises. Not going global with their society wouldn't make sense.<br /> <br /> Now, they <i>can</i>be somewhat diverse, but ultimately it is making them isolated or even insular that doesn't make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T11:56:45-07:00","id":1479663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479602#post1479602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also don't seem to be appreciating the time frames we're talking about. You're talking about cultural exchange between cultures that are basically only a few centuries old (France in 2022 is not anything like France in 12222), while many of the Garou Tribes have changed exceedingly little over thousands of years. If you went back in time 500 years, to the place you live now, people wouldn't be speaking the same language (though yes, similar) and would be a vastly different culture from what you're used to. Modern France would definitely seem a lot more relatable to you than that. A Silver Fang can go back in time 5,000 years, communicate easily, and find that the &quot;alpha&quot; Tribe really hasn't changed much in general attitudes and philosophies.<br /> <br /> Yes I focused on moon bridges, because that's about different Septs and how easily they can access each other for exchange and trade. The Garou have lots of other tools that make cultural drift less impactful than it is in humans... like the ability to just ask your great-great-grandparents how they handled things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you are right, there is indication in the books that tribes didn't change that much, and Garou Tongue didn't change that much and so on. And sure, having contact to ancestor spirits is part of that. On the other hand, there are Renewalists amongst the Silver Fangs, too. And the tribes changed do to an shift towards more homid in their ranks.<br /> <br /> In any case, I'd love it, if the Setting would shift back to focus more on septs that differ from another and Garou focusing more on local problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479602#post1479602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301240#post1301240\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...40#post1301240</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479602#post1479602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But also? The US doesn't actually have particularly strong stereotypes around most European cultures. Why isn't there a Tribe with Portuguese stereotypes? Because aforementioned US writers didn't actually have any stereotypes about Portuguese people to base a Tribe on. There isn't some idea of Portuguese culture in the US cultural mindset. There's a reason why US stereotypes around eastern Europe are about a giant area of the continent and not individual countries and cultures: people here don't know enough to even start to form more specific stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479605#post1479605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> covered well the Ghost Dance. About &quot;<b>Council</b>&quot;, this is the default translation for the terms the First Nations actually use in North America to define their inter-tribal organizations. They had this kind of institution to help ease relations between tribes or reduce violence in times of war way before the American settlers arrived, and currently still keep Tribal Councils as inter-tribal organs to help ease relations and pool resources where they need it.<br /> <br /> So while we don't know what will be made of them in the game yet, at first Ghost Council makes a lot of actual sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting.<br /> This information should be in a side bar and there should be a disclaimer that &quot;Ghost Council&quot; is the best estimate translation into English, but possibly there should be also names in first nation languages given, to showcase that the name is language depended and several members of the tribe might call the tribe by different names.<br /> <br /> It may be that in German the two words got conflated, that kind of thing happens sometimes. But in English (and Portuguese, I can attest), they're really distinct, and while subtle the distinction is <b><i>extremely</i></b> important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479605#post1479605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't ask a random. There are things like representatives and consultants. If you want to go cheap you seek a representative, a person that takes on themselves the responsibility to understand their own group as much as possible to bridge this kind of gap, either as voluntary work or hired by some governance body within the group. If you want to be certain you hire a consultant, a person whose work is precisely to help you understand what you need to understand for your purposes.<br /> <br /> Those are professionals being paid to do the heavy-lift of proper a study, not random people being interviewed in the streets. And they're not that hard to find and hire, even with the caveat of wanting specifically consultants on a given ethnic group no one sought out before. Which is not the case with the First Nations, instead they keep <b>several</b> certified bodies of consultants and even free services for consultation on cultural implications.<br /> <br /> All minorities and countries I know of have those kinds of services because being understood is kind of our goal. The only way to not know that such services exist is to never have asked, which is perfectly fine for you, who're just discussing things in a forum, but is inexcusable for a media company talking going global with their IP and putting money on it. Consultation is a minor cost that should just be a part of the process.<br /> <br /> If you're interested in, countries generally have such services at their embassies or equivalent outpost, they help authors, scholars and potential travelers to their country, most actually help anyone who asks, at least in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that. Still, I imagine, that two consultants might come to different conclusions regarding a given topic. So, I totally see that the today, when reworking the games, such services seem like the best way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479605#post1479605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of Asian players would like the same as you, actually, I don't know if they're a majority or not (but i have a guess). But here Paradox already made their mind as it seems and you won't be happy with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479605#post1479605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, the point isn't in the specific numbers. Werewolf established too soon that the Garou have a hugely stable culture, with little change through time, they share most myths and the core of their religion, they have a global spanning war in their hands, and they have access to several tools to ease interactions between them. Those are global premises. Not going global with their society wouldn't make sense.<br /> <br /> Now, they <i>can</i> be somewhat diverse, but ultimately it is making them isolated or even insular that doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>They share myth, sure. Most myths, not necessarily. Like I said, there are hundreds of thousands of local legends. It is said that, even in prehistory, it took several long meetings and still the whole bunch of negotiators had to move the meeting to Pangea to condense tenets out of the legends. <br /> Sure, it is also said the Litany is a whole bunch of stories and songs, presumably shared amongst all the tribes - but possibly not, since it is said to take a lifetime to master it. And the Silver Record is also valid for all the tribes. But that doesn't negate the possibly infinite number of stories local to septs.<br /> And, sure, the garou share a cosmology and the essence of their religion is shared among the tribes, but as you point out, the garou have had contact with each other over the ages and the core elements of their religion, the Triad, Gaia and Celestines therefore remained a stable factor in all tribal mythology.<br /> <br /> In the end, it is speculation, weather or not the garou's means of travel etc. would allow for cultural differences between septs or not, since it is a fictional setting, not a case study in anthropology. But, if you can ask your great-great-grandparent, who they handled things, and the answer might be: &quot;We did this and that, but my daughter didn't like it, so she and a bunch of her peers left and conquered their own land to rule.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T13:17:54-07:00","id":1479666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479663#post1479663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, I'd love it, if the Setting would shift back to focus more on septs that differ from another and Garou focusing more on local problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>The essential problem is that there are only two effective ways to do this:<br /> <br /> 1) Reboot it so you can allow this to be more naturally the case. Maybe nWW/Paradox should have just done this from the start, but their attachment to the cWOD brand drove them to not want to take this option.<br /> <br /> 2) Use the metaplot to radically change all the elements in the setting that cause a more standardized culture within the Garou Nation. This is obviously Paradox's preference on things so far, but it's also been rather divisive in the fandom because it means Paradox is picking which aspects of the setting get kept, and which get axed instead of trying to support a broader range of preferences. BNS's take on WtA was geared in many ways towards making local things more unique - or another way to look at it is would be to say to enable local LARP groups to do their own things while still being able to participate in one of the larger LARP network - but most of those changes are not well received by TT focused groups.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Interesting. </div> </div> </div>I... guess?<br /> <br /> Even with increasing globalization of human culture, most cultures don't have direct and consistent exchange with one another. Sometimes this results in one-way exchanges (some countries tend to export a lot of culture and thus there's the seeds of stereotypes being spread around without a return; lots of people consume US made media while the US doesn't import media from those countries at anything resembling reciprocal rates), and sometimes there just isn't any. I'm confident you could go to any place on the planet, pick two far off countries, and ask the people what's the difference between people in those two countries and you'd get blank stares. Do you have strong ideas about how Lithuanians and Latvians are different? What about Bolivians and Paraguayans? Laotians and Cambodians? Even if you personally have strong ideas about this, how many of your neighbors do? Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, I imagine, that two consultants might come to different conclusions regarding a given topic. </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> But consider that the main two potential results of such differing conclusions are:<br /> <br /> 1) Most people of the relevant cultures think that putting in the effort was good enough and aren't going to hold it against a company that the experts can't agree.<br /> <br /> 2) The company gets credit for consulting an expert, but it's clear they should hire the other one next time; creating a greater awareness of which experts have a better sense of what the real people they're trying to communicate the cultures of feel about things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T05:13:38-07:00","id":1479686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479543#post1479543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Native Americans IRL specifically asked to drop it. Not by far as intensely as they asked to drop <i>Wendigo</i>, but still. Yes, it is offensive.<br /> <br /> Main reasons:<br /> <br /> 1 - Only those two tribes used their patron's name directly as tribal name. While apparently subtle, this is a fine example of exoticization;<br /> <br /> 2 - The authors had zero understanding of what the spirit meant in its original culture and general cultural context, just used a White Pop Culture understanding of it without ever consulting a Native opinion, which is problematic in several levels;<br /> <br /> 3 - It broadly applies to all Natives a name that actually belongs to only one tribe, without regards to any nuance on how diverse and distinct the cultures of the several Native nations are. It is as if there were only two European Tribes called Broxa and Chernobog.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see that the discussion developed further, but I want to adress this message because it was quoting me, and because I also want to add to the discussion my Italian perspective of an Italian living in Italy.<br /> But as a foreword, I want to say that by no means I intend to dismiss the problem as non-existent.<br /> I'm actually trying to understand better how people in USA are perceving such problems.<br /> <br /> First of all, something I didn't know was that the native IRL asked specifically to drop it. So I'd say what was right to do was surely to drop it.<br /> <br /> I don't have a solid opinion on exoticization. In 90% of pop culture products, Italy is exoticized.<br /> Really, it's to the point of silliness and ridicoulness almost all the time. But it's not a big deal to me.<br /> I've met really few people that decisively lamented about it. When it's about us we usually roll our eyes up or sometimes even enjoy a laugh about it.<br /> I'll also add that I always liked the Giovanni as they were, despite some of the terrible implications of the stereotype of them.<br /> My humble opinion is that any author that decides to place some of their suff in another country will be inevitably victim of some kind of exoticization, because story takes place in another country exactly because it feels more exotic that way.<br /> I firmly believe that works of fiction shouldn't be taken as a textbook. Any kind of fiction should be taken with a grain of salt, so to speak.<br /> <br /> But italians weren't genocided by the people the author comes from until less than two hundreds years ago (which is a very short time frame if we think about it), so there's that to take into consideration for the specific case.<br /> <br /> I personally think Rein-Hagen &amp; Co. had the best of intentions regarding the matter, but they didn't have the resource and easy access to information that there is today back in 1991. So the original authors shouldn't be criminalized as they did intentionally something very wrong. They were just born and grow up in a life that was a bit out of touch with such problems.<br /> <br /> So, I'll stop talking about the specific case from here on because I came to the conclusion that dropping the name was the right thing to do.<br /> But I have issues with this idea that exoticization is plainly wrong by itself.<br /> I mean, my personal opinion is at a minimum degree it's kind of inevitable once you decide to set a story very far from home.<br /> Also, somewhere in the world there are people that might like exoticized stuff. Or stuff that wasn't meant to be exoticized but certainly it is from an outsider point of view.<br /> For example we should ask some japanese players if they preferred Vampire when the myth of Caine was more centric to the setting due to Rule of Cool, or if they prefer it now as more agnostic.<br /> <br /> I will say again, I'm not talking about the specific case because I think it is being handled in a good way. I'm talking about exoticization in works of fiction for broader and more general cases.<br /> <br /> To give an example in recent times: Shang-Chi movie was sort of a flop in China.<br /> Apparently, at least from what I gathered, the supposedly cultural aspects and myths were handled very badly at the end of the day, despite the flag of representation being held high by the producers.<br /> So, apparently it was still best intentions but also exoticization to the max<br /> <br /> I don't see too much difference in what's being done sometimes today than what Rein-Hagen &amp; Co. did in 1991: best intentions, not-so-great execution.<br /> So I think such problems must be addressed, and also the debate must go on<br /> <br /> I saw in a post earlier some talking about White Knighting.<br /> I'll add to the debate that one of the perceived stereotypes about USA is that on this matters USA has a tendency to White Knighting the whole world.<br /> And the other perceived stereotype about USA is that USA people understand little of the outside world (as someone else already brought up here about the cultures of Europe and the fact that they are simple not known in USA).<br /> I think for this kind of debates to go further that this USA perception of themselves should be addressed (if it's not a stereotype perception from outside, that is). Otherwise it will always be exoticitazation to the max (but again, is it really that serious an issue? My personal guess is that a lot of people in the world just shrug and think: &quot;Eh, Americans.&quot; when that kind of exoticization happens to themselves)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T08:27:07-07:00","id":1479697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479686#post1479686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To give an example in recent times: Shang-Chi movie was sort of a flop in China.<br /> Apparently, at least from what I gathered, the supposedly cultural aspects and myths were handled very badly at the end of the day, despite the flag of representation being held high by the producers.<br /> So, apparently it was still best intentions but also exoticization to the max</div> </div> </div> </div>No, at least from the reviews of it I've seen. It had to do more with Shang Chi being not unfamiliar enough to be a draw, because the rest of it was too run of the mill compared to martial arts action movies from China. It's a concept that CJ Leung of Cool History Bros labeled <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gjl-p7B_o2s\" target=\"_blank\">the Cultural Uncanny Valley</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T10:36:04-07:00","id":1479717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479697#post1479697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, at least from the reviews of it I've seen. It had to do more with Shang Chi being not unfamiliar enough to be a draw, because the rest of it was too run of the mill compared to martial arts action movies from China. It's a concept that CJ Leung of Cool History Bros labeled <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gjl-p7B_o2s\" target=\"_blank\">the Cultural Uncanny Valley</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon is notable for being a very boring and paint by the numbers movie in China.<br /> <br /> Humorously, THE LAST SAMURAI was known as a Ken Watanabe movie in Japan with Tom Cruise considered the ethnic comic relief.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T15:06:35-07:00","id":1479749,"title":"","content":"While I might get into the bigger post later, a point of order:<br /> <br /> Shang-Chi has yet to be released in China. You can't really call a movie a flop with an audience that hasn't gotten a chance to see it, and has had almost a year now of their government saying it's bad representation of Chinese values as to why they aren't allowing it to be distributed there (even if outside of China a lot of people assume it's because the Chinese government is using it to punish the Chinese diaspora community that's highly critical of said government by targeting Western made films that have lots of ethnic Chinese influence behind the camera).<br /> <br /> The Cultural Uncanny Valley effect is still worth considering for how to handle WoD topics, but lets make sure we have data on an given work's popularity/reception to go off of.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T16:24:35-07:00","id":1479758,"title":"","content":"A quick post.<br /> I just want to apologize about my Shang-Chi mistake<br /> I double-checked and even found the articles I remembered<br /> But I remembered them incorrectly!<br /> The flop movie the articles that I've read were talking about was in fact Mulan, not Shang-Chi.<br /> In the same articles they talked about Shang-Chi too, hence my fuzzy memory.<br /> And indeed Shang-Chi hasn't been released in China yet, and maybe it won't be, due possibly to censorship of the chinese government. Allegedly the chinese government said the chinese cultural aspects are bad represented or mistaken, BUT given it's the chinese government talking and we're also talking about censorship I would definitely take the governement's opinion with a big grain of salt.<br /> So, very sorry about my mistake.<br /> Still, I agree the Cultural Uncanny Valley is definitely worth considering","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T21:34:58-07:00","id":1479782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479686#post1479686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a solid opinion on exoticization. In 90% of pop culture products, Italy is exoticized.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, I think you brought some really good observations, I'll just add some points.<br /> <br /> I'm a Brazilian living in Brazil, so my actual personal experience with exoticization is similar to yours, despite nowadays I'm being one of those grumpier types that don't like to accept this shit. But the bigger problem isn't for us (at least not directly), but for people from our countries or descendants of those living there. Or people from other countries living in ours. That's when those problems become RL problems.<br /> <br /> Also, context matters, and here it means the corpus of media a work is inserted in. There's a huge difference between a given group being played as exotic when they're frequently represented in more grounded ways, from when they're almost always represented as exotic, even if the work itself is the same. Exoticization isn't the mere show of a culture as difference, but the regular and systematic representation of that culture as some kind of fantastic prop instead of people.<br /> <br /> Other than that, mostly agree. Talking about the mess of the original setting matters to contextualize, but we can only blame the authors for this past so far. After all, with all the problems it's still a setting that managed to gather Brazilians, Italians, Germans, Japanese, Koreans, just to name a few nationalities in this forum, to discuss those games 30 years after publication. What really matters is that the authors from <b>now</b> can't commit the same mistakes, they don't have an excuse anymore.<br /> <br /> The part about the US White Knighting the whole world is certainly a common perception, and by what I see of US commentators I think it is indeed real. And the part on Mulan, it was partly the problem of not hiring a proper consultant, instead AFAIK they gave the production team a time to go to China to &quot;learn local culture&quot;, but didn't hired any Chinese to work on production proper, just as actors. So they had American writers, American producers, American directors, and an almost touristic American view of China. Also it was partly just the movie being bad, plain bad. Like, the animation wasn't very ethnic accurate, but it was fun. The <u>live action</u> movie is boring, and no cultural accuracy will change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":"for clarity. 04-30-2022, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T22:40:41-07:00","id":1479788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479782#post1479782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The part about the US White Knighting the whole world is certainly a common perception, and by what I see of US commentators I think it is indeed real. And the part on Mulan, it was partly the problem of not hiring a proper consultant, instead AFAIK they gave the production team a time to go to China to &quot;learn local culture&quot;, but didn't hired any Chinese to work on production proper, just as actors. So they had American writers, American producers, American directors, and an almost touristic American view of China. Also it was partly just the movie being bad, plain bad.<b> Like, the animation wasn't very ethnic accurate</b>, but it was fun. The movie is boring, and no cultural accuracy will change that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Ravnos may have been referring to articles on the more recent, live action version that really, really shat the bed across the board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T00:13:20-07:00","id":1479791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460916-werewolf-5th-edition-information-in-crimson-thaw?p=1479788#post1479788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Ravnos may have been referring to articles on the more recent, live action version that really, really shat the bed across the board.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, me too. I was making a comparison. The animated movie is fun. The live action movie is boring. I'll edit for clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}